<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">The Love of the Game</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, December 1, 2000 by <a href="mailto:whitefox@eqrants.com">WhiteFox</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Do most people love games? Most likely not... most "gamers" like games... they don't love them though... Me? I love them... I'm of the few... the elite... the hard-core gamers. Actually, I'm still searching for people who love games to the same extent as me... I'm devoting my LIFE to games... Some would think... "What a waste"... but the way I see it, if you love it, what&#8217;s the problem with devoting your life to it?<br><br>Most people think of games as something to fill your time when there is nothing to do... Some think of games as something to do whenever you can spare the time... and some think of games as something to do 24/7.<br><br>As I said, I'm still looking for someone who loves games to the same extent as me... the same <b><a href="http://www.penny-arcade.com/view.php3?date=2000-07-07&res=l" target="_blank" >level</a></b> as me. Only people who come close would be Gabe and Tycho down at <b><a href="http://www.penny-arcade.com/index.shtml" target="_blank" >Penny-Arcade</a></b> but since I don't really know these people... the search continues. Eventually I'll meet someone with the same love for games as me.<br><br>Now, I love games, I play games 24/7... is that all there is to it? Hell no... I love the whole ritual of buying the game... bringing it home... unwrapping the plastic that&#8217;s always a bitch to get off... opening the book and smelling that new book smell and finally putting the CD in my computer/console to see if it should be treasured or broken with a hammer. Damn... who needs women!<br><br>But what drives people to play games? Most people play games for enjoyment, pride, or competition. For me, it depends entirely upon the game. Most games I get some form of enjoyment... games like StarCraft where I've seen every unit a million times... cast every spell a million times... I play more for competition. Then games like Final Fantasy, I not only play for enjoyment but for the pride of saying "I did every mother fucking thing there is to do in that game" and knowing its true.<br><br>I get the "There is more to life ya know" a lot... all I got to say to that is, more what? Going to a football game? After playing games for years upon years I don't consider watching a football game an "exciting" experience? Going to the movies? Watching TV? Nice, but still not horribly fun compared to the interactive movie that is gaming. This is what I have chosen to do with my life... and damn, its gonna be fun. I don't have some delusional dream of getting into the NBA like most of the sport morons out there... lets face it, your never gonna do it all. I find games to be the most enjoyable part, so I'm going to spend most of my time with them.<br><br>Games... gotta love em... I would take a bullet for my computer... less I had the money to buy another... if that was the case I'd bum rush the fucker while he shootin my computer and show him a new level of pain.<br><br>Love games? Hate Games? <b><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=749" target="_blank" >Comments?</a></b><br></p>
