<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Sacrifice</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, November 29, 2000 by <a href="mailto:whitefox@eqrants.com">WhiteFox</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Good Morning everyone! I wanted to talk to you about a demo I downloaded recently. Sacrifice. This strategy game is becoming very popular very quickly... I love StarCraft and all but if my friend isn't on to get a 2v3 going there really isn't any challenge in doing 2v2's or 1v1's with my other pals... Since my "one" friend is the only other person I know that is good enough to even attempt a 2v3 I'm kinda screwed without him. So... I've been looking for a new strat game to play when he isn't on... I'm still getting RedAlert2... but I downloaded the demo for Sacrifice lately because its attracted a lot of attention... a lot of good word on the street about this game if you know what I mean... well... I'd say the word is very much on the dot. The graphics... simply beautiful... not only that, but its one of the FEW games where it can be high-end and low-end. The graphics are VERY much scalable... I'd say min-req for playing this game decently is probably a p300 with a decent vid card (shit on the box is ALWAYS wrong). Not that I have this prob... I slammed all the graphical options up to 100% and got a beautiful play. Its a very simple game, and very fast paced. The only real problem I see with it, is that its VERY defense oriented. Its much better to let your enemy come to you, trash his army, and counter when he has nothing. Since there are no resources... you can very easily do this. No reason at all to leave your base... in a game like starcraft if the person goes hard defense and waits for you, all you do is expand and contain... wait till you have soooooo much money... and he has jack... and then just crush him. In this game, you really don't have much reason at all to leave your base...  I see a lot of room for frustration. This seems to be a common complaint though... the game is still awesome, very basic game play, easy to understand. I picked it up in what... 10 minutes? Probably less ;P Then again I play games for a living.<br><br>If you haven't seen a screenshot from this game (you under a rock or something?) go ahead and click the <b><a href="http://www.zdnet.com/gamespot/filters/products/screens/0,11105,914208-97,00.html" target="_blank" >link.<br></a></b> <br>Am I getting this game? Yup. X-mass. I'm in that horrible boat where your not allowed to buy a goddamn thing. Everyone makes you stick it on your list and you gotta wait till X-mass.<br><br>Now if you wanna go download the 90 meg demo of "Sacrifice" go ahead and click the <b><a href="http://www.zdnet.com/gamespot/filters/products/0,11114,914208,00.html" target="_blank" >link.</a></b> If your not gonna buy it its well worth it to at least download and try it. <br><br><b><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=724" target="_blank" >Comments?</a></b><br></p>
