<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Strategy Games...</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, November 27, 2000 by <a href="mailto:whitefox@eqrants.com">WhiteFox</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">How to play? Question that&#8217;s debated daily in almost every strategy game chat room out there. Rush or go for the long run, with the occasional newbie screaming DEFENSE ONLY!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<br><br><b>1) NO RUSH 10 MINUTES</b> A common belief is that its "Gay" to attack until both players "agree" that its time. Otherwise your a rusher.<br><br><b>2) RUSH HARD</b> Another belief is that you have to kill them fast, rush! Some take this to the EXTREME with builds so fast that if they fail mean almost certain death.<br><br><b>3) ECON FIRST </b> Others think "rushing" is fine but prefer to go for the long run. Get a good econ going and work from there.<br><br><b>4) DEFENSE ONLY </b> The newbie who builds nothing but static defense and has a record resembling 3-142.<br><br>Now, what&#8217;s correct? Well. I can say for a fact that DEFENSE ONLY is incorrect. You will never win this way.<br><br>"NO RUSH 10 MINUTES,&#8221; type games... I guess these are fine if you like them but they aren't the way the game is designed to be played. These games don't have timers that keep you from attacking for set time. These games are usually just so newbies don't die in the first 10 seconds of the game and give them a chance to tech to the strongest unit in the game.<br><br>What about RUSH HARD? Not my cup of tea but I think rushing is fine, as it will almost always get you killed vs. any non-newbie player. I prefer econ first, units second. Getting 5 units and then losing them in a failed rush and having no money to build more is not a position I prefer to get stuck in.<br><br>Thoughts... <b><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=712" target="_blank" >Yours?</a></b><br></p>
