<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">The Day After</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, November 24, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Thanksgiving is over. Most of us spent the day with family and loved ones. We enjoyed good food, good company and perhaps a beverage or two with friends. You may have played with your little cousins or nieces or nephews and realized that you just aren't as young as you used to be. At the end of the day you may have sat around and watched some TV and saw the real horror of Thanksgiving. The in-your-face complete commercialization of Christmas.<br><br>No matter what you do or where you go today you are going to see ads for Christmas sales. Department stores will be trying to outdo each other with decorations and special holiday sales to try and get you to spend your hard earned money at their particular store. Beer companies put cutesy commercials on to try and get you to drink their beer for the holidays. A lot of stores actually started putting their Christmas stuff up before Halloween was even over. <br><br>Quite frankly it makes me sick.<br><br>We live in a time where nothing can just be enjoyed for what it is. A holiday movie comes out and there are toys and accessories launched everywhere. God forbid they can just release a movie and have you go enjoy it. You also have to enjoy action figures and stuffed animals related that are spawned from the movie.<br><br>Christmas comes around and it cannot be celebrated as a religious holiday. All it is now is a reason to buy gifts and throw our money back into the economy. Do you think many kids today even realize what Christmas is supposed to be about? I am not going to say I am the most religious guy in the world. But growing up I went to church every Christmas and always knew there was more to the holiday then just gifts. As the years go on that is becoming more and more forgotten. <br><br>It's a shame, really.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=697"><b>Agree? Disagree? Don't Care?</b></a> </p>
