<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Info on a New Verant Game, And It Doesn't Sound Like It Will Suck</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, November 7, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Daily Radar has a <a href="http://www.dailyradar.com/features/game_feature_page_1765_1.html"><b>story</b></a> on a new game that Verant is working on called Planetside. You can read all about it right <a href="http://www.dailyradar.com/features/game_feature_page_1765_1.html"><b>here</b></a>.<br><br>Now I am no big fan of Verant. Some might say I am the anti-fan. But this game actually sounds like it <i>might</i> be fun! For those of you too lazy to go and read the story at Daily Radar, here is a brief run down of it.<br><br>It is a tactical MMOFPS (that is Massive Multiplayer Online First Person Shooter). It is like a TFC server with 1000's of people instead of like 16. It is team based and there are 4 teams to fight for. You can improve your character and but not to such levels that you will have an unfair advantage over everyone else. It is basically a big old deathmatch with some extras that you dont' find in Quake.<br><br>I better stop this or I might get accused of being a Verant fan. Anyway, I encourage you to go read about this game. If you are into TFC or Counterstrike then this might interest you too.</p>
