<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Weekend Notes</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, October 30, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">There are some Mondays when I come in to work all fresh and ready to tackle a new week. There are some Mondays when I come in and I am ready to scan the EQ newsgroups and messageboards and websites, looking for just a little tidbit about Verant that I can post here on the main page.<br><br>Today is definitely not one of those Mondays.<br><br>To me, a pretty sure sign that you are getting just a little bit older is when you go out and get drunk on a Saturday night and pay for it all day Sunday. I am not just talking about having a hangover. I am talking about getting sick throughout the course of the day. I am talking about still feeling the effects of it on Monday. I know I have developed somewhat of a reputation as a bit of a drinker. Jokes are made about it on the message board and it's all in fun. But maybe it is true, maybe I do drink a bit too much. Maybe I am asking for trouble and should reevaluate things to determine if my present course is self destructive. <br><br>Nah, screw that! I am having too much damn fun!<br><br>Saturday I spent 2 hours at a Downtown Detroit tavern drinking Guinness. After that I spent 3 hours at Joe Louis Arena watching the Red Wings kick the hell out of the Columbus Blue Jackets. Who's idea was it to call a team the Blue Jackets anyway? We decided that 'Blue Jackets' is a bit too long of a name and we just started calling them the bj'ers and made fellatio jokes all night. Anyway, throughout the course of the game I, of course, drank. At that point you really don't care that you are paying $7.00 for a beer, you just want the beer guy to keep bringing them to you. The biggest disappointment of the evening is when they stopped selling alcohol with 10 minutes left in the game. At that point I decided our best bet would be to leave and find <b>MORE ALCOHOL</b>.<br><br>We made our way to our local bar, basically our own personal Cheers. Where everybody knows our name and everything. It was their Halloween party. Perfect. What better excuse to drink then a Halloween party. A bunch of people you know dressed up in goofy costumes. Of course I drank more, a few shots here, a few beers here, a few shots mixed with beers. Yes, I was drunk and talking to anything remotely female that I could find. Luckily there weren't any guys dressed up as females for Halloween, at least I don't think there were. One girl thought it would be fun to discuss drugs. After informing her that I was clean and had never even so much as smoked, she ran down the laundry list of various illegal substances she had tried. It amazes me, the things people will do when alcohol is so readily available and legal!<br><br>I think the capper on the evening is when I decided it would be a wise idea to play darts. My vision is normally very poor, but when you can't actually see the dart board then I think you know you have had too much to drink. I threw the darts once or twice then decided the effort just really wasn't worth it. If you ever think you have perhaps had too much to drink, try throwing darts. If you can't see the board, or if it appears to be moving back and forth, then you know it is time to call it an evening.<br><br>I eventually made it home safely and paid for my actions on Sunday. But that is the way it goes though right. Nothing is for free, even an exciting weekend packed with thrills and spills.<br><br>I know this post is probably unnecessary and self important. I am just bored and decided to give everyone a little peak into the secret life of Buur. Exciting eh?<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=398"><b>That was my weekend, how was yours?</b></a> </p>
