<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Gordon/Whineplay Stuff</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, October 25, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Gordon got a little pissy on the <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/025960.html"><b>Whineplay</b></a> board about the current state of the forum.<br><br><font color="#00FF00">Hello all,<br>I've been a little disappointed at the reception that's been given thus far to Absor. Rampant and insults seem to have returned, meaning that we're going to have to again ramp up the enforcement of the rules again. We've let things slide a bit over the past week, and cannot allow it to continue. We will not let these boards once again deteriorate to what they once were back before we added accountability to the posts people make here. <br><br>I haven't had as much time as normal to spend reading and responding to issues here given my new responsibilities, but I'm going to make the time to come back and help move things along while Absor comes up to speed. Please be aware that we will continue to enforce the board rules, isible under the FAQ at the link at the top of the page.<br><br>Common courtesy and decency are not concepts reserved for us as a company towards you as the players. Continued flaming and insults are not acceptable content here on the boards. We want Absor to be more of a "man of the people" than I was able to be, because that is what the players have indicated that they want, but please remember that this is a two way street, and only you can make this happen.<br><br>Thank you,<br><br>-Gordon</font><br><br>So Gordon moves on to a new position and Absor isn't quite up to speed on the boards yet. Don't you think that maybe Absor should have been fully trained and then let loose on the boards? While Absor was being trained Gordon could have kept his board duties and there would have been no down time on board moderation. Nah...now that would have made sense. The Verant way of doing things was to give Gordon a bunch of new responsibilities and start training Absor at the same time. That way the boards could go to hell and then Verant could bitch about the players abusing the board and such. That makes a lot of Verant sense.<br><br>What I will really be curious to see is how they will manage to make Absor a "Man of the People". I guess Gordon was unable to lower himself to "The People", thus he couldn't fill that role.<br><br>More on Absor/Abashi and fun on the boards in the days to come. God help us.</p>
