<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Things I Haven't Had Time To Do</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, October 18, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I am hopelessly addicted to Baldur's Gate 2. I am spending every free moment I have playing this game. If I was as dedicated to my job as I was to this game I would be climbing up the company ladder rather then just holding it up so people can climb ahead of me.<br><br>This game is seriously that good, at least in my opinion. I thought Torment was the best RPG I had ever played but I am seriously starting to have doubts about that now.<br><br>I thought I would better explain my current addiction by mentioned some of the things I have been putting aside to clear more BG2 time.<br><br><ul><br><li><b>Laundry</b>.  My clothes are starting to respond by name at this point. I can't possibly spare 2+ hours to get my laundry done when I could be using that time rescue Jaharia from her curse.<br><br><li><b>Food</b>. The best thing about a good game addiction is that it is an incredible way to lose weight. Who can think about food when you have to free child slaves!!<br><br><li><b>Housework</b>. Empty soda cans and beer bottles are perfectly fine examples of table art. Crap laying on the floor just keeps it from looking boring and unused. It also prevents visitors from spending the night at your apartment and possibly taking up precious playing time.<br><br><li><b>Friends</b>. Who needs them when you have Minsc and Boo.<br><br><li><b>Work</b>. Nevermind that one, I always do a half-assed job at work anyway.<br><br><li><b>EverQuest</b>. What is that game again? And wasn't I supposed to be starting a guild or something?!<br></ul><br>Those are just some of the examples of things that I have been neglecting. I would go into the personal hygiene issues but I really don't think anyone needs to read about those issues.<br><br>Remember, this is just after playing it for a week or so. I fear how things will be a couple of more weeks into the game.</p>
