<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">You Won't Have Gordon to Kick Around Anymore</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, October 16, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Thanks to my wonderfully consistent internet connection I missed out on this story when it broke, of course. Ah well, you can always count on EQ Rants to bring you the best second hand EverQuest news on the net. Well, second best may be stretching it, but regardless...<br><br>Gordon Wrinn has a new position at Verant. Yes, you heard that right. He is no longer the Community Relationships Manager. He is now in charge of coffee and donuts. Wait, my sources are telling me that he actually got a position on the Live Team (as opposed to the dead team, who by all reports really haven't gotten a lot done).<br><br>You can read about it yourself <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/024394.html"><b>here</b></a>.<br><br>Taking his place is Alan VanCouvering. Welcome to the team Alan. You can count on being harassed here just as much as anywhere else. Maybe I'll drop a few questions Alan's way to see if we can get to know him better. Then again after some of the e-mails I got after the last <a href="http://eqrants.com/abashi.htm"><b>fluff interview</b></a> maybe that isn't such a good idea.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=255"><b>Your comments?</b></a> </p>
