<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Power Outage</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, October 10, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">News brief here for you:<br><br>*cue newsticker sound in the background*<br><br>Hello, I am an_internet_newsperson here with an EQ update.<br><br>A number of EverQuest servers went down last night when the power was unexpectedly cut. Fans of EverQuest were reportedly 'really upset' with this and vowed to terminate their accounts unless Mystere was reinstated. Wait. I am getting word that this is a seperate story.<br><br>Gordon Wrinn, Verant punching bag, had this to say.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">I apologize for the short poweroutage experienced on several of the servers. I've read all of the complaints regarding UPS systems, etc., and I'd like to ensure everyone that our setup is sufficient to handle *most* forms of power outages. <br><br>Unfortunately, this one wasn't covered by "most". An electrician working in the data center cut power between the source, and the servers. The point at which the power was cut was between the backup sources and the servers, so our substantial battery backups and generator power never came into play.<br><br>I believe that this is the first or second power-related outage of the service since the time it's been up, so suffice it to say that it's not a usual occurance. <br><br>Thank you for your patience</font> <br><br>When asked why only some servers were effected by this outage Gordon responded by saying that 'A number of the servers are at another site.'<br><br>Reportedly, CompUSA was upset to learn that Verant is using a few of their display model PCs as EQ servers. When asked for comment a_compusa_spokesperson said, "It really is a shame that they can't afford to keep servers at their own location. We asked them to stop and they told us 'Shut up and give me my ten bucks per month, little man. My Porsche needs some performance upgrades.' I guess we know where all thier money goes now."<br><br>*end newsticker*<br><br></p>
