<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Final Thoughts</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, October 9, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">There has been so much said about this Verant/Mystere situation that sites are running out of adjectives and sentences to describe it all. You have seen tireless coverage from <a href="http://lumthemad.com"><b>Lum</b></a> and from almost every other EverQuest site out there. The fan fiction that caused all the trouble is posted right here on <a href="http://eqrants.com/fiction.html"><b>this very site</b></a> (get it while you can...it may not be here much longer). There has been quite a few statements from Verant, statements from Mystere, statements from the President, debates by the Presidential candidates, Senate meetings and so on. I am, quite frankly, pretty sick of this whole story.<br><br>Unless something huge happens, which I can't imagine at this point, I am done with it.<br><br>Mystere has <a href="http://vnboards.ign.com/message.asp?topic=7192109&replies=8"><b>made peace with Verant</b></a> and I think that should be good enough for the rest of us. I am in no way absolving them of their crime here. I just don't think that there needs to be anything else said on the subject. They made a grave error in judgement and almost the entire EQ web community made them aware of that fact.<br><br>I am going to venture a guess here and say that you will never, ever, see Verant in a worse PR nightmare then the one they just created. That is ashame for those of us that base their websites on pointing out flaws and ranting about Verant decisions. I just don't think VI can afford many more incidents like this. With Star Wars Online looming ahead and the inevitable announcement of EQ2, they just can't afford to continue look like such giants buffoons in public. They are going to have to look like giant buffoons in private for now on.<br><br>I mean come on, just how many times can a company manage to make itself look like an ass and still to keep a loyal customer base? My guess is not too many more.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=160"><b>Your guess?</b></a> </p>
