<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Roleplaying is a bannable offense</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, October 5, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">This story has been covered elsewhere but I have had a couple of requests for my opinion on it. Being the "People's Webmaster" that I am, of course I am going to comply.<br><br>Everquest is supposed to be a roleplaying game. A roleplaying game involving thousands of different players each with their own idea of how they like to play. Most people never bother with the roleplaying aspect though, instead choosing to play the game as the hack and slash fest that it is. It's hard to roleplay when 90% of the player base doesn't even know what roleplaying is. There have been many requests for role players server, a request which Verant repeatedly turns their head on. They think that the team servers are good enough. <br><br>Despite these facts, some players still do choose to roleplay. Some dress up in EverQuest outfits and go to official functions, some run roleplaying guilds and some post roleplaying stories on newsboards.<br><br>One of those acts is a bannable offense.<br><br>Mystere posted a <a href="http://vnboards.ign.com/message.asp?topic=7048656&replies=7"><b>roleplaying story</b></a> on an IGN message board. The site was in no way affiliated with Verant and this story should not have had anything to do with them. The story was a graphic description of Dark Elves, yes the evil, vile dark elves, torturing and killing a couple of High Elves. Wow, in the realm of roleplaying that sounds real far fetched eh?<br><br>Verant apparently saw this story and thought it was so graphic that they banned the author. Yes, they banned someones account for writing a story on a non-Verant messageboard. This isn't an act that was played out in game. This was someone taking the time to write a story and then being banned from EverQuest for their efforts.<br><br>Do you need much more proof that Verant hates you?<br><br>Gordon, god bless him, had this to say on the subject:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Like all other account issues, this is a matter between us and the owner of the account. It's not something that we're going to discuss or justify publicly. <br>We make determinations based on information at hand regarding who is or is not having a positive affect on EverQuest's community. If we determine that one person's actions make EverQuest a game that other people do not want to play based upon those actions, we will excercise our right to refuse service to the extent necessary to provide a reasonable and enjoyable gaming environment.<br><br>This is the extent to which we'll address this specific issue. If people have general questions not related to the specific issues in this case, I'll be happy to field them tomorrow. This issue is however closed.<br><br>-Gordon</font><br><br>So there you have it. If you do something on a message board that Verant feels '<i>is not having a positive affect on EverQuest's community</i>' you too can be banned. If Verant feels that my website, or say <a href="http://lumthemad.com"><b>Lum's</b></a> website, are not having a positive affect on the EverQuest community then they can just ban us and be done with us. I would have included <a href="http://tweety.bowlofmice.com/tweety/"><b>Tweety</b></a> in that list, but Verant already banned her. So be careful what you post on boards, or what you say to friends, or what you write in your diary. Verant is watching and they are ready to ban you.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=90"><b>Message thread started by someone else. Comments?</b></a> <br>(note: I am getting some indication that <a href="http://vnboards.ign.com/message.asp?topic=6102849&page=1"><b>this</b></a> is the actual story he was banned for. It doesn't matter. It is still just a story Verant.)</p>
