<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Clarification</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, October 4, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I never feel the need to defend my site or myself. But I saw a comment on EQ Vault from one of their readers that I really wanted to respond to.<br><br>As per usual, when Kithias sends in a new EverSticks, I write a few of the news sites and ask if they will mention the comic. I don't do this to draw traffic to my site, well maybe a little bit. Mostly I do it so that more people have a chance to read EverSticks. I owe Kithias that much for bringing his comic here.<br><br>One of the readers at EQ Vault left a little comment regarding the comic and the site:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Don't go there.. not worth it. Very weak attempt at making a comic. Furthermore why Rant when you can play another game.. I give this site two thumbs down for having the least information for EQ.</font> <br><br>First off, I happen to think EverSticks is a very good comic, which is why I asked Kithias to allow me to post them here. There are many more people who enjoy it then don't.<br><br>Secondly, I want to clear out a little misconception that people might have. I don't <i>hate</i> EverQuest. Yes, amazingly enough it is true. Does anyone honestly think I would spend this much of my free time working on a site dedicated to a game if I didn't enjoy said game at least a little? I write this site because:<br><br>A) It is fun for me.<br>B) Because there are flaws in EverQuest and I won't stand by as a paying customer without pointing them out.<br><br>Many people stand idly by while others make decisions that affect them. I am not one of those people. I have an opinion and I am going to voice it. You may agree with me, you may not agree with me, but you have to respect my right to have an opinion. The people that sit and say nothing are half of the problem (the other half being Verant). When you just take things as they are and don't demand change then things never change. Pretty simple eh?<br><br>As far as my site having the least EverQuest information, well no shit. I am not like the other sites, ok? I want to clear that up right now so that no one gets a false impression of what I do here. The day you come to this site see an item database, character guides, information on trades skills or spell lists is the day I have officially sold out and I should be shot. The reason the Trueshot Longbow Quest info is still on the site is because I wrote that a long time ago and it has a meaning for me. On days that it seems Verant will never get their head out of their ass, I read it and remember that I once really enjoyed this game and that I may enjoy it that much again.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=77"><b>That is enough of that rant. Feel free to leave your own comments.</b></a> </p>
