<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">More bad PR</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, October 2, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I rarely read <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/ubb/everquest/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro"><b>WhinePlay</b></a>. I actually loathe that message board and do what I can to avoid it. Today I decided to check it out and I pulled this <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/020008.html"><b>this gem</b></a> out right away. <br><br><font color="#FFFF00">I just wanted to call attention to an unfair situation. <br><br>A friend of mine was banned (7 days) without warning while playing her level 1 gnome on the new server. After sending an e-mail to customer support asking why she had been banned, she was told that it was because her station name was deemed offensive. She explained that she had chosen it after ten other names had been rejected and she had grown frustrated, and she said that she would be happy to have it changed if there were any provision to do so. She has gotten no response and is now planning to quit permanently out of sheer frustration.<br><br>When she chose her station name, there was no rule against offensive station names. She had no way to change the name after the rule was created. It seems entirely unfair to ban her without giving her any opportunity to rectify the situation.</font> <br><br>We are not talking about a character name here. We aren't even talking about a chat handle. This is a Station login name, that if everything goes the way it should, no one else should ever know. Despite the fact that no one would ever even get the chance to be offended by it, Verant suspends the player without giving the player a chance to change it to something more suitable for Verant.<br><br>I can understand them banning players for picking an offensive player name in game. They want to keep it safe for the kids I suppose. But when you start banning players for something that has zero chance of ever having an effect on anyone else, you are just proving that you really do despise your player base.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=59"><b>Got something to add?</b></a> </p>
