<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">GameFan Goes Down</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, October 2, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">As you have probably seen reported on many other websites, the GameFan network has folded. A few EverQuest sites were effected by this, including EverCrest, /gu comics and EQ Answers.<br><br>GameFan has been in trouble for a while. They haven't paid their hosted sites in months and never gave a justifiable reason. Just ask Lowtax over at <a href="http://somethingawful.com"><b>Something Awful</b></a>. He went months without recieving the payments he was owed for putting add banners on his site. He was forced to switch networks and sign up for individual banner deals.<br><br>The days of making money by running a fan website are coming to an end. Unless you are selling some sort of product or a service, you just aren't going to make money. Banner clicks just don't generate revenue because most people just ignore them. Even when they don't ignore them, they generally aren't going to buy anything from the site. The companies kicking out the cash for web banners realize this and they aren't going to be willing to pay out big bucks for web advertisement. It just doesn't pay off in the end.<br><br>Fans sites will become just that, fan sites. Run by people who enjoy the rigors of making a website and then hoping that people will like to read what they have to say. This site qualifies as a fan site, although I am sure Verant doesn't think of me as one of their biggest fans. I don't make a dime and never lived under the false pretense that I would. My server costs are covered by the fine people at <a href="http://atomicrhino.com"><b>Atomic Rhino</b></a> and that is it for benefits that I recieve. <br><br>Just in case you were wondering.<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=56"><b>Get a comment?</b></a> </p>
