<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Station Break</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, September 28, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">There are a couple of interesting articles over at <a href="http://www.station.sony.com/stationbreak/"><b>Station Break</b></a>. From what it looks like the articles are there to somehow try to convince you that EverQuest is actually a roleplaying game of some sort.<br><br>Here are a couple of excerpts with my comments:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">There are two forms of quests in EverQuest. The first is referred to as the "static quest." This is a hard-coded quest that remains in the game for an indefinite period, and runs independent of human game master control.<br><br>The other form of quest in the game is the dynamic quest. These events are the sovereignty of the Quest Masters, and can often lead to massive changes in the game world. They are performed in the game just once, and then become recorded history. They require the assistance of the Game Masters and volunteer Guides, as well as a specialized team known as the Quest Troupe to enact.</font><br><br>I think they forgot the 3rd form of quest in the game. These would be the broken quests. The ones that don't work and yeild nothing but frustration. These would also appear to be the players favorite quests, as you often hear them mentioned on <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/cgi-bin/forumdisplay.cgi?action=topics&forum=General+Discussion&number=2&DaysPrune=10&LastLogin="><b>WhinePlay</b></a> and other public forums.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Ever wanted to know who that elf chick is on the cover of the EverQuest game boxes? She is Firiona Vie, the central figure to the world of Norrath. As Chosen of Tunare, Firiona must try to reunite the forces of good. Each character depicted on the EverQuest box, for or against Firiona, plays a crucial role in the developing story of EverQuest.</font> <br><br>The developing story of EverQuest? What story would that be? The never ending story of nerfs, bad Public Relations and game bugs? If this elf girl is somehow responsible for all that then I want her head on a platter! Screw complaining about Gordon or Brad, they just told us who the <i>real</i> culprit is! Down with Firiona Vie!!! Die Vie! Die Vie!!<br><br><a href="http://forums.eqrants.com/showthread.php?threadid=32"><b>Comment link. I haven't started one on the new board yet and this seems to be as good a time as any.</b></a> </p>
