<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Installation is hard</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, September 28, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Sometimes I am real thankful that I run this site and that I don't write for someone else. The reason being that I can come on here and bitch about whatever I want to bitch about, and there is no one looking down from above complaining about what I choose to rant about.<br><br>Having said that, I am going to once again bitch about Comcast@home. Yesterday was my cable modem install date. Finally after over a month of problems this was all going to be taken care of.  Nevermind the fact that they completely inconvenienced me by saying that they would install sometime between 7:00 a.m. and 6:00 p.m., I was gonna have cable!!<br><br>Here is the chronological order of events leading up to the installation time for the cable.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">* 5:30a.m. - Woke up completely hung over, showered and went to work. Over an hour early. I have no idea why I did that.<br><br>* 7:30 a.m. - 11:30 a.m. - Went through the motions at work and came up with a reason to leave before I got sick. Staying out late, drinking heavily, combined with coming into work ungodly early for no reason does not leave one feeling well.<br><br>* 12:00 p.m. - Got home and met with the lovely young lady that was staying home waiting for the cable guy for me. She was suffering from a hangover also so we layed around complaining and waiting to get sick.<br><br>* 1:00 p.m. - Paydirt! Cable guy arrives ready to install the cable. Runs the line and says he will be back in 15 minutes, with his partner, to finish the install.<br><br>* 1:15 p.m. - No one arrives. I start to get drowsy.<br><br>* 1:15 p.m. - 4:00 p.m. - Fall asleep on the couch trying to avoid getting sick. Cable guy never comes back or calls.<br><br>* 4:10 p.m. - I call cable company bitching. They assure me that everything is cool. Right....<br><br>* 5:00 p.m. - Cable company calls me back saying they will be over in 15 minutes. Where have I heard that before?<br><br>* 5:15 p.m. - Cable company calls again saying that they are extremely sorry, but that due to an account error on their part, my cable modem will not be getting installed.<br><br>* 5:16 p.m. - I get extremely irrate and start bitching and yelling at cable company asking how in the fuck this can happen.<br><br>* 5:20 p.m. - They say they are not sure what happened. I ask how they intend to fix it if they don't know what happened. They assure me it will be fixed. I ask again what the problem is. They say they don't know. I say "So you have no idea what the problem is, you wasted my whole day, and you expect me to believe you can get a mysterious problem solved and get me my cable modem within the week?" They say "Yeah, it's crazy..."</font><br><br>So, once again, craziness has taken it's toll on my life. I cannot get internet access because 'it's crazy'. I kid you not, they told me that they have no idea what the problem is. None. I could understand if it was a problem with the cable line or something, but they screwed something up in their computer system that is preventing me from getting pron at 150MB/minute. And they don't know how to fix it.<br><br>So, to sum up the day: I was hung-over, didn't get my cable modem installed, the site went down for hours, Verant deleted all my precious level 1 newbies, and I got no fresh pron.<br><br>How was your day?</p>
