<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Stratics Sucks</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, September 18, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Yesterday EQ Stratics posted a story about a bard sit-in. That's all fine and dandy because they are, you know, a news site. The problem I have is when they follow it up with stuff like this:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Posting the news of this event does not imply any support by Stratics for this event. News is posted by Stratics as a service and does not necessarily reflect the views of stratics.com or its staff.</font> <br><br>What the fuck is that about? Seriously? Are they so concerned with their relationship with Verant that they can't post a tiny article about a player sit-in without having a disclaimer saying that they are pansy asses who suck up to Verant (yes that was a run-on sentence). They weren't posting a long commentary from <a href="http://www.geocities.com/tweetyrant/"><b>Tweety</b></a> about how screwed up Verant can be. God forbid you actually support a show of solidarity from Bards, who are currently in the running for "Most Nerfed Class of the Year".<br><br>Some of the crap that happens on the web really boggles my mind. If you ever notice this site leaning in that direction, please just shoot me.<br><br><font size="2" color="#FFFF00"><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000046.html"><b>Posting the useless garbage of that website does not imply any support by EQ Rants for that website. Commentary is posted by EQ Rants as a service and most certainly reflect the views of EQ Rants and its staff.</b></font> </p>
