<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Todays Headlines: Rangers getting a fix, Hell freezes over</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, September 12, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Brad McQuaid made this statement on the <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/013021.html"><b>whineplay boards</b></a>.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">After a LOT of internal testing, interacting with the community, and major debate, we've decided to upgrade Rangers as follows:<br>We will be upping their dodge and parry to near Warrior levels. I don't want to get into specifics yet because we are still fine tuning, but the end result is that a Ranger should be significantly more survivable. <br><br>I'm personally happy with the solution because, rather than just increasing defense and making them more Warrior-like, we've upped skills that are more traditionally associated with Rangers (the view that they are nimble, chain-wearing fighters who often avoid attacks).<br><br>I'd also like to pre-announce a future goal and policy change:<br><br>Soon (we'll announce a date in the future), we're going to completely stop adjusting game balance as it relates to tweaking classes. Recently, we've made more changes than usual due to the level limits being raised from 50 to 60. Soon, however, we're going to come to a point where it stops. <br><br>We'll continue to add content (i.e. items, spells, etc.) and game balance will still be tweaked (and will continue to be tweaked as long as we do add content). But class balance changes as a whole will cease.<br><br>The Ranger upgrade is part of this. I'd say that hopefullly by early 2001 we'll be done.<br><br>Abashi or I will post more on this as we work out the plan in detail internally.<br><br>-Brad</font><br><br>This comes after months of complaints that the Ranger class pretty much sucks. It's nice to see Verant actually do something that the players request, of course it would have been nice to see them look into this when the problem was first noticed a few months ago. I guess it took SunMoon quitting to actually get VI to get their collective asses into gear. <br><br>I am going to wait until they officially announce what will be changed before I praise them or bash on them. Knowing Verant there is very good reason to assume they will screw this up somehow. But I don't want to jump to conclusions.<br><br>Oh, and in case you missed it in Brad's statement, soon all classes will cease being balanced as VI is apparently sick of people complaining and then having to, you know, actually fix stuff. We'll probably see this last until the next major MMORPG hits the market.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000034.html"><b>Rangers Rock!</b></a> </p>
