<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Ranger Plight - Part II</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, September 7, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Brad "We Listen and Consider Issues" McQuaid <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/010994-2.html"><b>chimed in</b></a> with his thoughts regarding the SunMoon/Ranger issue. You can read SunMoons rant <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/010994.html"><b>here</b></a>.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">The Live team is focussing on the FA style quests now, and then will move on to some serious dungeon retuning. <br><br>How much time they allocate to Ranger tuning is up to Jeff and I know he's talked to Sunmoon about it. <br><br>Frankly, while I have a lot of respect for Sunmoon and his comitment to both EQ and the Ranger community, I found his post a bit shocking, especially since Jeff Butler called him personally on the phone and spent some time talking to him about issues. <br><br>With a subscriber base of 280k plus, I thought his call was a pretty good indicator that we're listening and considering issues and I'm disappointed to see such a rant :(<br><br>-Brad</font> <br><br>Disappointed to see such a rant, Brad? Are you somehow unaware that a lot of people are disappointed that you seem to ignore current player concerns in order to get out your next money making expansion? Here is a challenge for you guys at Verant; why don't you focus your team on getting stuff fixed now, then when you have that done release Velious. Nah, there is no money to be made that way is there? You'll release your expansion, which will introduce more bugs, which will never get fixed. It's an endless cycle that will never change so long as Verant has their silent majority to stand by. You know, the ones that don't frequent boards and just play the game to play? They are the ones that don't bitch, praise or say anything about Verant. Crazy, but they do exist.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000031.html"><b>Bah, we join this thread already in progress.</b></a> </p>
