<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">The Rangers Plight</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, September 6, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">High level Rangers are screwed up, or fucked up if you will. Everyone knows this. They are a mana drain. Keeping them healed enough to be useful is such a waste of mana that the clerics would rather they not participate in their groups.<br><br>Their offensive output is nowhere near high enough to counter their lack of defensive protection. They are a melee class that can't tank, which makes them useless. Their spells aren't strong enough to use as a primary attack and archery, well archery is a joke.<br><br>This has been brought to Verants attention many, many times. Their response? Standard stuff really, they don't see the problem and so the problem must not exist. <br><br>SunMoon Glademaster is probably the most recognizable Ranger outside of Brad "We aren't giving exclusive screenshots to websites yet" McQuaid. Sunmoon runs <a href="http://eqforge.com/ranger "><b>The Rangers Glade</b></a>, the be-all, end-all of Ranger websites. SunMoon has had enough and rather then stay and wait for Verant to make changes, <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/011282.html"><b>SunMoon canceled his account.</b></a> <br><br>This is the type of thing that should make Verant open up their eyes, unfortunately they won't. They have stated that if Rangers fill their role, then they can still be a solid class. But what is their role? When you can't tank effectively, can't heal effectively, can't cast effectively and can't solo at all, what good are you? How can you fill a role when the only things you are best at, tracking and archery, become useless to a high level group. Why would you want a Ranger in your group to track when you can have a Druid do it and also fill a healer role.<br><br>It is just amazing to me that Verant can look at their player base, spit in their eye, and tell them to have a nice day.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000031.html"><b>But what do I know, I am just an idiot rant site webmaster with an opinion. Oh yeah, did I happen to mention I play a ranger?</b></a> </p>
