<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">EQ Emulater = Verant Unhappy</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, August 31, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">J. from over at <a href="http://www.drtwister.com"><b>The Dr. Twister Network</b></a> sends word that Ashran of <a href="http://www.hackersquest.gomp.ch/"><b>Hackers Quest</b></a> has been getting cease and desist orders from John Smedley, CEO of Verant, for producing an EQ Emulator. You can check out the info over at Doc Twisty's <a href="http://eq.drtwister.com"><b>EQ page</b></a>.<br><br>This is pretty interesting, no one has successfully created an EverQuest emuluator up until this point. There were emulators for Ultima Online but Origin never really made a big deal about them. Verant, on the other hand, seems hell bent on stopping this immediately. But then again they often seem hell bent on stopping fun too...<br></p>
