<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Online Store = Mission Impossible</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, August 31, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Brad "The Real Deal" McQuaid (don't know where The Real Deal Came from, it just sounded good) gave us this nugget of info regarding the online store:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Unfortunately, we're running at least a couple of weeks late :(<br><br>We're still setting up proceedures with our distributor and tweaking things -- we REALLY want to do this right this time without any hitches. <br><br>That said, in my opinion it's taking too much time, and I apologize -- for what it's worth I'll do everything I can to accelerate the process. <br><br>-Brad <br><br>ps. the good news is that it's being set up so we can sell not just the Kunark upgrades but also t-shirts, hats, posters, figures, etc., which should IMHO be pretty cool.</font> <br><br>Because as everyone knows, setting up an online store is real hard. I mean, it could take months, even years! By the time we have the online store available we will be ordered EverQuest 5. Of course it will be shipped late and they will forget the CD Key or something.<br><br>But seriously, it is rather ridiculous that it has taken this long, and that it is now being delayed again. To make matters even worse, you can't order Kunark by phone or anywhere else for that matter. The more cynical among us might believe that this is Verants attempt to make you go and buy a full version from retail stores. Full version = more $$. Although I have covered this in a previous rant.<br><br>But hey, look at the bright side. When the store is available you will be able to order EverQuest t-shirts, hats, boxer shorts, bottled water and glow-in-the-dark condoms.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000027.html"><b>Come get your EQ merchandise right here!!</b></a> </p>
