<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Milo's final words</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 29, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Milo, being the sentimental oaf that he is, decided to send in some final words to Everlore. <br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Hello Catalyst! Ask Milo was loads of fun for me on several levels, and I appreciate all of your first-rate attention to my requests, suggestions, and textual edits. The column is indubitably something on which I shall look back fondly. <br><br>To the public, I can only say that I'm a little surprised and very grateful that the number of people who lament the termination of the page so outnumber the high-fiving lummoxes. I guess that more people understood what I was doing, and what I was about, than I figured. Thanks everyone, you rock, all o' yous. If you ever run into Mymm Cynyny on Veeshan, or Cindysaurus on Luclin, give me a wave! <br><br>/quit... </font> <br><br>Well, at least he left with a parting shot. I thought people like <a href="http://lumthemad.net"><b>Lum</b></a> and myself were 'whiny dorks', now we are reduced to <a href="http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?va=lummoxes"><b>lummoxes</b></a>. Well I called him an oaf and I would rather be a lummox then an oaf so HAH!<br><br>And remember, Ask Milo will always live on here at EQ Rants. If you have a question you would like to have Milo answer just send it to  <a href="mailto:askmilo@eqrants.net"><b>askmilo@eqrants.net</b></a>. </p>
<a name="newsitem967499410,1098,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Gordon backs off</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, August 28, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Everone's favorite sock puppet, Gordon, rescinded on some statements he made yesterday. He said he was going to check with the programming team to see if items that were stored in unproper containers, i.e. sewing kits, quest bags, etc., could be destroyed once someone logged out. You see, by doing that Verant can punish those players that have the audacity to be smart.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Hello all,<br>The original thread on the Partisan pack shifted later to a topic about combinable containers in general. I wanted to separate out the two issues and discuss them individually. I've started a separate thread on the issue concerning the unannounced change of the partisan pack, which is a bag given by an NPC for the purpose of completing a quest. <br><br>In this thread I'd like to discuss my comments where I said:<br><br>"Concerning items in combinable containers, I think that I'm going to chat with the programmers Monday and see if they can make the containers eat any items in them upon logoff/Linkdeath. I think that there'd be no question of the intent of those bags then."<br><br>After reviewing this post that I made earlier, I do agree that it appears to be a threat when viewed out-of-context, and understand the general reaction that followed. The point of the post was to respond to multiple posts from people earlier in the thread who had no idea that they shouldn't use combinable containers, particularly free bags given by NPCs to complete quests, for general item storage.<br><br>I'd thought that the number of people using the bags for this purpose were the exception rather than the rule, an observation that was apparently mistaken given public response to my post. Given that public response, we won't be taking any steps to "destroy" items in combinable containers upon logout or linkdeath.<br><br>I do apologize for the way my response was phrased and hope everyone understands that neither I nor other members of the tuning team actively seek out ways to make the lives of the players more difficult. <br><br>-Gordon</font><br><br>I especially like this part "neither I nor other members of the tuning team actively seek out ways to make the lives of the players more difficult". Nah, constant nerfings, class balance problems and general bugs don't make our lifes more difficult. They sure do make our gaming experience much less enjoyable though.</p>
