<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Nerfs, aren't they grand? or, Oops, we screwed up again.</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, August 24, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I was diligently scanning the new and improved <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/cgi-bin/forumdisplay.cgi?action=topics&forum=General+Discussion&number=2&DaysPrune=10&LastLogin="><b>Official EQ Message Board</b></a> (now with 37% less whining!) when I came across this <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/007576.html"><b>gem</b></a>:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">As of this patch 99% of Veeshan's Peak loot became NO DROP. I have no problem with the change, even though I think the idea of NO DROP is a lame shortcut for shortcomings of the game, but I digress, anyhow, the items in question were ALL made NO DROP without ANY warning. Items we had in storage can no longer be given to their proper owners.<br>I can only imagine what would happen one day if people logged in and saw that the Ykesha was made NO DROP without even so much as a PEEP from the development team. <br><br>This isn't good business, plain and simple. Give people a warning at least a patch in advance when you make such a large scale change to item structure.</font><br><br>Abashi, god bless his soul, came back with this well thought out and helpful explanation.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Erm. Sorry about that. Those changes weren't supposed to go in until next week, at which time we would have given some warning. <br>-Gordon</font> <br><br>How in the hell can you make a mistake like that? Gordon once promised that all item changes would be announced, repeat ALL ITEM CHANGES WOULD BE ANNOUNCED, and something like this slips through?! I could personally give a rats ass less about Veeshan's Peak items, I am no where close to being able to go there, nor will I likely ever see it. But I do expect Verant to not totally screw things like this up though.<br><br>Well, let's give them a chance, maybe next patch they will change it back. Oh wait, another gem from Abashi:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">We won't be changing the items back, so that would pretty much leave establishing a trade window in which the two servers that have visited Veeshan's would have an opportunity to trade the items with the assistance of a GM. However, that would run afoul of our policy for not getting involved in nodrop item issues. So now the problem at hand is seeing what exception, if any, we can make.<br><br>-Gordon</font> <br><br>You know what, screw your damn policy for once. You screwed up, plain and simple. Is it that hard to own up to your mistakes and correct something that you did wrong? I guess in Verants case that answer is a resounding yes.<br><br>In all fairness, if Verant does fix it I will write a follow up article....but they have given me no reason to have faith in them.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000023.html"><b>Comments, I know you got some...</b></a> </p>
