<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">The Horrors of Miss-Con</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, August 23, 2000 by <a href="mailto:whitefox@eqrants.com">WhiteFox</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I'm sick of getting my ass kicked by some critter that&#8217;s been green for 10 levels. I found out last night that my necro can't take a skele when he has only 1 bar of mana and no pet. Level 16? Wtf? I got a goddamn RTS, I should kick the damn things ass! Instead its miss miss miss while this skele that cons green is wham wham wham for 20 a pop. My Wiz gets this a lot, he has died more times than I can count to a pack of greenies because they jumped him right after a battle when he was OOM. Now I know a skele is only green by about 3 or 4 levels to my 16 necro but jeez... My wiz gets eaten alive like that by stuff that IS 10-15 levels green. <br><br>Now what really pisses me off is that Gordon is over there sitting on his ass saying that its a group game and stuff is supposed to kick your ass when it "Looks like a reasonably safe opponent"<br><br>Now... we all know that&#8217;s bs because I've found that it works the other way around. Every now and then you come up against that critter that cons even or yellow but is easy as fuckin hell to take. You know what I'm talking about, you just hit level 14-15 and you found you can eat gorge hounds who con white-yellow alive only to be mauled to death by green lions after the battle (my wiz)<br><br>Now... on to the really bad form of Miss-Con. The one where you con something and it shows green so you attack and all of a sudden it cons red. I hate that bug... Not a good bug on a PvP server. I once accidentally attacked a wizard who was 6 levels higher than me. Can you say, BBQ? Not often but every now and then...<br> <B><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000022.html" target="_blank" >Got Miss-Con?</a> </B><br></p>
