<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Name Filter</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 22, 2000 by <a href="mailto:whitefox@eqrants.com">WhiteFox</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Thought I'd drop a small rant on the name filter since I recently tried to create a new char. I hate EQ's name filter. Hate is the key word here. Never have any idea why the hell it is rejected.<br><br>As for fantasy names... come on people. You know how many fantasy books have been written in the past 100 years? Almost every name you can think of should be on that damn filter. I can understand names from FAMUS books like The Hobbit but Verant takes it to far. I typed in Terralock once and it got rejected. What the hell is Terralock anyone? Anyone know? Drop me an <a href="mailto:Whitefox@EQRants.com"><b>E-Mail</b></a> if this the name of a gun company or something. Its just a name I came up with on the fly and it got rejected. Yet again, Verant, must control EVERYTHING about the game down to the way you part your hair and yet have no responsibility for anything. Makes me sick.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000020.html"><b>Got something to say on the topic?</b></a> </p>
