<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Who is WhiteFox?</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 22, 2000 by <a href="mailto:whitefox@eqrants.com">WhiteFox</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Well... I'm a loud mouth living in SC, USA. I spend most of time at home. Gaming is generally, my life. I know a great deal about computers (considering I've never had training or course for any of it) and I've been playing games on them for years and years... The first game I can really recall is The Noid, followed by Night Shift, and finally Lemmings. As of lately I've begun to buy more and more games, sometimes several a month. I now have shelf after shelf filled with games ranging anywhere from Starcraft, to Half-Life, to Police Quest, to Worms. Why? Because I like games, more interesting than TV and hell of a lot more interesting that basket ball (least for me), which is just a really simple game (ball through hoop). Besides, the way I figure it, I've got a hell of a better chance at getting into the gaming industry than I do of getting into the NBA... still I know people who insist they will get in. I've recently begun to teach myself C++, and I plan to follow up with Python. I'm also a dedicated PvP player, I enjoy it a great deal. Don't get me wrong, I enjoy other gaming as well. Some of my all time gaming favorites would have to be Lunar, Phantasy Star, Wing Commander Series, FF7, AQ2, and probably StarCraft. Why do I play EQ? Because it&#8217;s one of the few games I don't feel that I've done all I can in, and its something to do while I wait for other games. <br><br>In my opinion for an online game to be great it must have both a good PvP atmosphere and good non-PvP atmosphere (EQ, tragically, doesn't really provide either of these). This is why I play, mainly, on one of the PvP servers. When it comes to PvP, I have no morals and no shame. I'm ruthless, and depending on my mood I scale my own challenge accordingly. If I want to take it easy I'll look for the easy targets. If I want a real fight I'll shout for a duel with someone around my level range. I enjoy setting the traps, thinking of how someone would react if I presented them with a certain situation and then try to correct for it. There are, of course, things I won't do, such as EXP PK. This doesn't mean I'm not nice. I don't go around screaming WHO YO DADDY or YOU SUCK while I'm hacking down people and I don't think I'm invincible like some people on the PvP servers... I get hacked down a enough and I often have conversations with people I've killed/been killed by talking about what could of gone different. Usually a lot more people bitching than actually controlling their temper and having a conversation... but I won't get into that right now. The way I see it if you play a PvP server you know the risks, you know what levels can attack you, and you know they could attack at any moment so don't have a fit when you get killed. I know a lot of people won't like me for this but that&#8217;s not my problem. The best part about being a PK is that you meet a lot of game designers... seems like half the people I kill claim to work for Verant Interactive and send me horrible threats about what they are going to do with their GOD chars. <br><br>Too prove my dedication to PvP I tossed together a quick picture from my UO days that can be found  <a href="http://whitefox.homestead.com/files/total2.jpg" target="_blank" ><b>here.</b></a> That&#8217;s a 200k picture. The file I have holding the rest is 7.6 megs and I didn&#8217;t begin taking record until the last year of my UO life. To prove my dedication to role-playing, and non-PvP things... well... I have no reason to. Considering how I own over 150 games (not even counting my console games) my favorite games consist of a lot more RPG and games where you can't kill other people than games where you can. In closing, I don't live to PK. I don't spend all my time doing it. Its just something that I do. I spend just as much time trying to get that damn last bubble as the next man.<br><br>That&#8217;s who WhiteFox is.<br></p>
