<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">What is wrong with this picture?</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, August 21, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I was browsing along the EQ Bitchfest today and I came across a post that bothered me. Check it out.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">On druzil ro, lately its becoming harder and harder to reserve the planes exclusively for your guild. We have approximately 9 guilds that can enter planes with somewhat success.<br>Here is this weekends schedule of events as I see it.<br><br>Friday Evening<br>Hate - Flames of Norrath<br>Fear - Imperial Guards<br><br>Saturday<br>Hate - Mythic Legion / HOSS wedding <br>Fear - L'malla<br><br>Sunday<br>Hate - Valiant Hearts<br>Fear - Mythic Legion<br><br>I'm making this post to throw out some ideas and in turn get some feedback. Possibly come to some type of consensus on rules, we as guilds, can follow when reserving the planes.<br><br>Some ideas.<br><br>1) Planes Reservations seem to encompass a whole day. Would it not be make sense to reserve within 12hour blocks? This adds approximately two more reservable blocks to the weekend that some of the PST guilds could capture on.<br><br>2) If it all possible only schedule one plane per weekend.<br><br>3) Post on this global forum when reserving a block. That way we all have one post to make. </font> <br><br>That just doesn't sit right with me, having to schedule to do a raid just doesn't seem right. At that point the game just doesn't seem fun anymore. It is work. I look forward to someday doing a plane raid, but I'll be dammed if I plan on doing it based on a schedule. "We are sorry Buur, the Plane of Uberage is booked solid for the next few years. Check back in 2005. Or shortly after the online store is up, whichever comes first."<br><br>Scheduling gold and dinner is one thing...but online games...hmmm...<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000019.html"><b>Comment link, in case you care to, you know, comment.</b></a> </p>
