<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Patch Rant</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, August 18, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Welcome all, today I have for you a drug enhanced patch rant. No, not illegal drugs, but drugs of the prescription variety. And I am aware that I am a day late with the patch rant. I apologize. Well not really, deal with it.<br><br>As always, I yanked out the stuff that I didn't feel like mentioning. Once again, deal with it.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">August 17th, 2:00pm<br>------------------------<br><br>*Updated Patch Message*<br><br>Some additional changes were included in today's patch that were not listed in the patch message earlier today. This patch message is a replacement for the one posted earlier:</font><br><br>Because doing a patch message correctly is hard.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*Miscellaneous Changes*<br><br>- /trackplayers now supports a "GROUP" option, allowing trackers to exclude all player characters, except ones in their current group.</font><br><br>- Does me no good. I can never find a group to begin with. I am starting to think people loathe me.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The EQCLIENT.INI has some new features, including one allowing logging (/log) to be on by default. Updated documentation for the EQCLIENT.INI file is at the end of this patch message.<br>- Activatable items, such as Journeyman's Boots, can now be activated by the corresponding number-key if placed in a hotbox.<br>- Items that are "out of charges" now display "Charges: None" when inspecting the item.</font><br><br>- That's nice. It's always good to know when an item becomes useless. I think half of the things in Norrath should always say "Charges: None" because I can't figure out a use for a lot of stuff.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- Attack-speed buffs and debuffs will now stack correctly. In other words, lower level spells will no longer overwrite higher level spells of the same type.</font><br><br>- Spirit of the Turtle will no longer overwrite Spirit of the Wolf. That is nice.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The "U" key (short for "use") has had its functionality enhanced. It now does the equivalent of a single left-click and single right-click at the center of the screen. In addition to opening doors, it will now consider and inspect PCs, consider NPCs, and use bankers, merchants, and guildmasters.</font><br><br>- I always thought the "U" key was short for U-Turn or something. I was always hitting it hoping to turn around and it never worked.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- Fixed the way that spell-effect icons are displayed on the UI. Previously, after adding several "buffs" to a character, one of the icons would be placed down in the chat window.</font><br><br>- kljlk;hujkhdsf,l;koiop[qi (sorry, the drugs caused me to pass out and my head hit the keyboard. I'll try not to let that happen again.)<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*Chat/Login Server*<br><br>This patch contains eqmain.dll, which is used by the EverQuest login/chat frontend. The following changes have been implemented:<br><br>- #help now accepts arguments. #help #command will return help for the requested command.<br>- Errors issued within the chat/login server frontend now display an "Error Number". Please have this error number ready when requesting technical assistance.<br><br>*Looking for Group Flag*<br><br>Players can now indicate that they are "looking for a group" by typing /LFG. This command will flag your character in both zone-specific /who lists, and the server-wide "/who all" list with "LFG". The LFG flag will remain active until you either enter a group or log out. Players can search for other players who are LFG by using filters in the /who command. For instance, to find rangers between level 40 and 50 who are looking for a group across the server, type "/who all ranger 40 50 lfg".</font><br><br>- Yeah, as if anyone wants a 40-50 ranger in a group. Sometimes I think Verant is really mocking us.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">It is our hope that this flag will make it easier for players to seek out group members, allowing for more adventuring with less preparation time.</font><br><br>- I think making soloing viable would go a long way towards allowing more adventuring with less preparation time. But what do I know?<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The Everquest Team</font><br><br>- The EQ Rants Team<br></p>
