<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Odds and ends</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 15, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Slow news day today, I can't find much to rant about. I could rant about how tech support people are totally useless if you ask them a question that isn't listed in the book that sits in front of their face. But I won't do that.<br><br>I could talk about how I got approved for my new apartment and will be in the process of moving shortly. And also I could say how frickin' excited I am about my new place. I could also talk about how it has a 24 hour indoor jacuzzi and a nice work out room. But I won't mention that either.<br><br>What I will mention is that support for the new guild idea seems to be pretty good. Some of you have seemed a bit distressed about having to leave your high level characters. Don't worry. It won't be expected that you spend all your time playing the new character. If your veteran character happens to be on the server we start on then that character is welcome into the guild.<br><br>I need some info from you guys. Everyone that is interested in this please send me a brief e-mail. 'For the subject put EQ Rants Guild'. In the body please say which server you would like to play on (I am not really sure which are split servers or whatnot), what race you would like to play, what class you would like to play, where you would like the starting point to be and what you had for dinner yesterday evening. Err...actually skip the dinner part.<br><br>That's about all I can think of, if there is anything important that I missed just throw a shoe at me or something.</p>
