<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Just a thought...</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, August 14, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I just got done playing Everquest, for like 5 minutes. I couldn't find anyone to group with so I got bored. I started thinking that it would be a lot easier if I was part of guild. Then I started thinking even harder! I could tell because there was a slight burning smell in the room, although that could have been my overclocked computer frying, but whatever. <br><br>Anyway, I started thinking that perhaps I could start *gasp* <i>my own guild</i>! I figure I have enough readers here to be able to start something. A bunch of us could start a new character on a different server and go from there. I know that the idea of starting over may not appeal to some of you, but you wouldn't have to play on the new server all the time.<br><br>I would have no idea what to call the guild, we would have to think of a name. But I could host a little guild site right here on EQ Rants with updates and stuff. It would be completely different from the main EQ Rants site. I am sure normal readers would be real excited to hear that we raided _________ (insert area there).<br><br>Let me know what you guys think? Is this something any of you would be interested in? E-mail me or post your thoughts right <a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000013.html"><b>here</b></a>.</p>
