<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Nothing original</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, August 11, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Sorry for not posting any original rants in the last two day. I decided to take a few days off from being creative. I sometimes need a break, don't we all. I will be back to original crap on Monday, but I figure a four day break isn't too much to ask.<br><br>I think I will repost the letter I wrote to John Smedley the day I decided to restart EQ Rants.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Mr. Smedley,<br><br>Hello. I am sure you don't remember my website or me. I once ran a very-very-very semi-successful EQ site named EQ Rants. I often took time out of my day to, well, kind of bash on your product. I liked your product but making a site that praises everything doesn't get a lot of hits. And plus I found enough flaws in it to keep me going for a while. Eventually I ran out of time because of a new job and canceled the website and my EQ account.<br><br>The reason I am writing is because I recently restarted my account because I am interested in playing your new expansion pack. Well much to my dismay I am currently unable to order the Ruins of Kunark because the EQ Store is not up. What I was wondering is if you could maybe send me a complimentary copy of RoK. In return I will restart EQ Rants and continue to bash on your product and, to be fair, competitors products every so often. I will also allow you to write a weekly guest column entitled "The Smed Man Says.." where you could give your opinions on any subject you want. It could be about food or cars or women, but I guess sticking with MMORPG's would be a little more on topic. I hope these conditions are suitable for you.<br><br>Also I saw that you are advertising for available jobs on your website. I think I could fill some positions nicely. I have quite a bit of computer background. I am currently the Webmaster at Henry Ford Community College (<a href="http://www.hfcc.net">http://www.hfcc.net</a>) and also a network troubleshooter. I am not particularly great at any one computer skill, but I have skills in many different areas. I am also a fast learner and I dress appropriately for the job. Please consider me as I think I would be a valuable addition to the Star Wars Online team, or any other team for that matter.<br><br>Thank you for your time regarding these matters. You can mail my free copy of RoK to the following address:<br><br>xxxxxxxx<br><br>Thanks again</font> <br><br>And no, he never responded to that one. I am certain I will be asking for a free SoV CD when it comes out too.......</p>
