<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">No Time</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, August 10, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I don't have time for a full fledged update or rant today, sorry about that. Instead I will leave you with a classic EQ Rants moment. Err..well it may not be classic, but it was the first thing I found in the archives that I thought was worth reposting.<br><br>This first aired July 21st, 1999. <br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Let's see, where to begin today. I really don't have a whole lot to talk about, so I will ramble on and see how long I can keep you with me. Oh, I made it to level 14 today and then at level 15 I get some new spells. Woohoo! It's a pretty sad commentary on ones life when he gets excited about magic being acquired in a computer role playing game. Ah, here is an idea, lets see what a day in my life would be like if I could live as my EQ Ranger for a day. <br><br>I would wake up in the morning, in a sitting position, and then I would go and <i>forage</I> for my breakfast. Maybe I could find some roots and a pod of water, maybe not the best get-up-and-go breakfast, but neither is Pop Tarts. I would then slip comfortably into my <i>banded armor</I> and brush my <i>minotaur axe</i> and be off to work. <br><br>I wouldn't be driving or anything, since I would have nothing to drive, and since there is no water between here and work I couldn't take the ever annoying boat (look at post on July 7th). I guess I would be stuck running, maybe I could ask my neighbor, I am pretty sure she is a <i>druid</i>, if she would cast <i>Spirit of the Wolf</I> on me. I would offer a couple of gold, just to be nice. Neighbor looks at me like I am crazy, hmm..she won't be getting my gold! Well time to sense my direction and be on my way. <br><br>Morning commutes are a real bitch so I would have to stop and fight a few of the locals who decided to cut me off, and what do you know...the guy conned blue so I gained some experience for my efforts, let's check his wallet. Woah! He has 5 gold, 6 silver and a leather belt! My lucky day! After that little detour I would be running late so I would <i>track</i> my way to safety and proceed on to work. <br><br>Damn, it is getting dark out...I had forgotten about how short an EQ day is and my having to run to work made me quite late. The boss is furious! A quick con and I see that he is yellow, not good news for me. I cast <i>Skin Like Wood</I> on myself and <i>Fire Protection</I> since the flames coming out of the bosses ears have me worried. I also decided to cast a <i>snare</I> on the boss, but wouldn't you know it...he resisted it. Damn spell never works when I need it. Seeing that I am not going to be able to avoid this one I spring into action with my trusty axe. Damn, my boss sure is tougher then he looks. I watch my life bar, that conveniently floats over my head, quickly start to diminish. Hmm...let's heal! Interrupted, interrupted, interrupted...ugh..hey wait, that one worked...oh Christ, only healed 10 points. That does me no good! Time to flee and mark this one as a day that I should have called off. Hmm..not gonna be that easy, the boss is quickly on my tail! Stunned. Dead. <br><br>I would be warped home with none of my equipment. Damn, it sure is gonna be a long walk to get all my items back, I sure hope the boss has gone home. Maybe the neighbor lady will reconsider that <i>Spirit of the Wolf</i>......<br><br></font> </p>
<a name="newsitem965844547,44949,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Patch Rant&#8482;...kinda...</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, August 9, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">What a dilemma. Here it is patch day, one of my favorite days of the week, and I can't find much to rant about. This patch is pretty good. I will give it a go anyway, just because I know that at least one of you enjoy the Patch Rants&#8482; (yes, I am trademarking Patch Rants&#8482;. If 'The Vision&#8482;' gets a trademark then so does Patch Rants&#8482;). As always, I will pick and choose what I want to mention. You know where to find full reviews of the patches.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">August 9th, 7:00am<br>------------------<br><br>*Guide Application*<br><br>The Guide Application is now back up at <a href="http://guideapp.everquest.com.">http://guideapp.everquest.com.</a>  If you are over 18 years of age, have a good customer-oriented attitude, enjoy helping your fellow player, and are interested in joining the Guide Program, we will be pleased to review your application.</font> <br><br>If you are interested in spending all your in-game time answering dumb questions, please apply. You'll maybe even get a free poster out of the deal.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*Kunark Users*<br><br>A new file, emeraldjungle_chr.s3d, is included as part of todays patch.  This patch adds additional displayable NPCs to the Emerald Jungle.  Please run the 'Kunark Patch' by pressing the 'Kunark Patch' button on the bottom of the patch program UI prior to entering EverQuest.~</font><br><br>Instead of hitting the 'Cancel' button that would probably save us all a lot of trouble.<br> <br><font color="#FFFF00">*Patch Day*<br><br>Greetings everyone! Today's patch contains some exciting new changes.</font> <br><br>Shouldn't they have said this before they started quoting patch items? I know, I am being nitpicky. <br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*General Enhancements*<br><br>- Rangers, Paladins, and SKs now have mana equivalent to that of a pure caster with the same stats.  This will give those hybrids a good deal more mana, regardless of their stats.</font> <br><br>- w00t! Suck it down casters!<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*Changes/Fixes*<br><br>- Small Studded Tunic recipe now works</font><br><br>- I'll just continue to eat foraged berries, thanks though!<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The Rusty Rapier now looks like a rapier.</font> <br><br>- As opposed to looking like a spoon or other kitchen utensils.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*Dragons?*<br><br>Rumor has it that some new dragons have been spotted in Kunark. It should be noted however that the dragons can be engaged from much further away than is intended.  Rather than hold off implementing these dragons for another week, we've decided to implement them now and fix the problem in the next patch.  Enjoy :)</font> <br><br>- Those rascals for Verant are letting us get away with something for a whole week! They are crazy I tell ya! Not that my level 19 ass could touch a dragon (Yes Findail, I am still level 19. Sucks eh?).<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">*Client Customizations*<br><br>Upon starting EverQuest, a new file (EQCLIENT.INI) will be created in your EverQuest directory.  This file contains customizable settings for:<br><br>- Colors for text messages in the in-game chat window<br>- Default screen viewing mode<br>- Default travel speed (run or walk)<br><br>RunMode - TRUE for run, FALSE for walk.</font> <br><br>- I could care less about the color thing. Blah, blah. But damn, is it nice to be able to default to run now. It really isn't that big of a deal to have to click on 'Run' when you log in. But it is really nice to be able to have it set as the default.<br><br>Another interesting point is that in the last Patch Rant&#8482; I mentioned something about a run default, and now it is implemented. Coincidence? Well ok, most likely. But for ego sake I will assume they did it just for me! <br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The EverQuest Team</font><br><br>- The EQ Rants Team<br></p>
<a name="newsitem965779198,95464,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">More notes from the new expansion</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 8, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I just scoped out the <a href="http://www.verant.com/press_releases.html"><b>official press release for Scars of Velious</b></a> over at Verant.com. They cover some basics, such as when the expansion will be released (Winter, 2000), pricing (still being discussed), number of new zones (16), and some other tidbits.<br><br>The thing that caught my eye was the breakdown of some of the new creatures. I'll just cut and paste here for you:<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">New frozen continent "Velious" located south of Antonica. <br>More than 16 new advanced adventure zones including: ice caves, crystal caverns, crypts, dungeons and frozen towers. <br>A new cast of visually stunning non-player characters including frost giants, ice dragons, snow orcs, cave bears, Snowfang gnolls, storm giants and vicious ottermen.</font><br><br>Ok, they had me with the snow type creatures. I'll buy into ice dragons, frost giants and snow orcs. Where they lost me was with the vicious ottermen. Ottermen? Vicious? Hmmm....<br><br><img src="http://eqrants.com/otter2.jpg"><br><br>Does that look vicious to you?<br><br>I will quote this directly from the <a href="http://www.nationalgeographic.com/ottercam/"><b>National Geographic OtterCam site</b></a>: <br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Found in or near rivers and wetlands throught the U.S. and Canada, North American river otters are powerful and graceful swimmers - and are known for their playfulness.</font><br><br>You read that! They are known for their playfulness! Not their ferocity or their viciousness! What are they going to do? Play Twister with you to death? Perhaps hide and go seek? Oh, I know, since they are river dwellers they will probably play a rousing game of Marco Polo until you drown. I certainly hope you guys know what Marco Polo is, if not that joke just bombed.<br><br>Anyway, I for one am just a tad bit disappointed in ottermen. <br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000012.html"><b>Walrusmen I could have handled, but not ottermen.</b></a> </p>
<a name="newsitem965736686,62744,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">"We kinda screwed up on the first manual, sorry" - Prima Games</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 8, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">In case you had the misfortune of picking up the 'Official Strategy Guide to Everquest: Ruins of Kunark' from Prima Games, you know what a complete joke it was. If you didn't pick it up, or you weren't aware that it was a complete joke, well then let me tell you something, it was a complete joke.<br><br>No, I don't think I could squeeze 'complete joke' into this update again. Wait, I just did. What a jokester I am. Hah! Sorry....<br><br>Anyway, Prima Games has released an errata on their <a href="http://www.primagames.com/info.php?ID=62"><b>website</b></a>. There are far too numerous items for me to list here, I will just go through it and pick out the good ones, Patch Rant style.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Pg. 18. Root: Change &#8220;an integral part of kiting a creature&#8221; to &#8220;an integral part of Root Blasting a creature&#8221;.</font> <br><br>Well, at least they are aware that kiting was nerfed. I wonder if they will cover nerfing in this errata. I kind of doubt it.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Corrections:<br>Barbarians can be Shamans, but not Shadow Knights.<br>Dark Elves can be Shadow Knights.<br>Dwarves cannot be Shamans.<br>Erudites can be Shadow Knights.<br>Gnomes cannot be Paladins.<br>Humans cannot be Shamans, but can be Shadow Knights.<br>Trolls can be Shamans, but cannot be Wizards.</font> <br><br>Damn, and a Barbarian Shadow Knight sounded so cool!<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Wood Elves forage; they don&#8217;t frag. </font> <br><br>Speak for yourselves! My Wood Elf owns j00 d00d! My r33t railgun skilz r0x0r!!!!<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Pg. 165. Races: Delete last sentence of second paragraph. (Erudite vision is as bad as that of any other race, but no worse than Human or Barbarian eyesight.)</font> <br><br>Thank god they changed that. They sheer idiocy of that statement just literally made me dizzy.<br><br>This list goes on, and on, and on, and on, and on, and...well, you get the point. There are probably quite a few dozen items I didn't mention here that got corrected. The idiocy of it all makes the book worthy of appearing as a special column over at <a href="http://somethingawful.com"><b>Something Awful</b></a> (By the way, if you have never visited Something Awful, I recommend doing so now. Well after you finish reading here that is. Hi Lowtax, link to me, k? And not in one of your awful links of the day.).<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000011.html"><b>If you bought this book, my condolences...</b></a><br>(They never did mention nerfing in this book.)</p>
<a name="newsitem965670099,25950,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">New zone, little excitement</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, August 7, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">In case you happened to miss it, Verant posted some <a href="http://everquest.station.sony.com/velious/screenshots/20000804/20000804.html"><b>screenshots</b></a> from their forthcoming expansion, The Scars of Velious. <br><br>Hmmm...not exactly the screenshots I would have picked if I was showcasing my new expansion. I mean, is that Everfrost? Are we supposed to get excited based on those pics? On top of that we already know there won't be any new playable classes and they aren't going to raise the level limit beyond 60. <br><br>So, what are we left with? An attempt by Verant to cash in a little more before the next round of MMORPG's come out. I, for one, am just a little disappointed. I mean, I don't expect much from them, but at least offer us more then this for our money. <br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000010.html"><b>Meesa thinks Verant's abeing greedy..</b></a><br><br>(I don't know why I just spoke like Jar Jar Binks. Maybe I am feeling a little more Star Warsy today with the passing of Sir Alec Guiness.)</p>
<a name="newsitem965650102,2388,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Free pron here?</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, August 7, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Today is going to be a bit of a crazy day for me. The boss is coming back after a two week vacation and I am sure to get in trouble for something. I don't really think I did anything wrong but as bosses normally do, he'll find something I did wrong.<br><br>Not only is work going to be crazy today, but I am going to apply for a new apartment. Having never applied for an apartment, I have no idea what to expect. I know they need to run some records on me or something. Make sure I don't have bad credit or whatever. Being as naive as I am if they told me they needed to do a body cavity search I would probably comply.<br><br>----<br><br>I installed a new tracking HTML code over the weekend. The other one I used just worked horribly, when it actually worked at all. This one keeps tracks of where referrals come from and stuff (thank you <a href="http://lumthemad.net"><b>Lum</b></a>). I noticed a ton of them came from people scanning Yahoo! and stuff for, get this, free pron!<br><br>Yes, apparently EQ Rants is not only your home for subpar ranting, it is also your home from free internet pron! Not too long ago I made a joke about being able to get free pron 24/7 on the net. Well now every pervert that scans Yahoo! and Google for free pron sites ends up at mine. I am sorry for the lack of pron here folks. I know I could probably get about 100,000 extra readers a month if I did something like that, but I wouldn't resort to such slimeball tactics. Would I?<br><br>----<br><br>Nothing really EQ related to rant about quite yet today. I didn't get a chance to play all weekend so I am not particularly fired up about anything right now. Give it a few hours, I am sure Verant will do something dumb.</p>
<a name="newsitem965426309,67251,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Board policies change = late afternoon update</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, August 4, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Usually I am waist deep in beer and women at this time on a Friday, but I saw this and figured it was somewhat news worthy. Actually I am normally just waist deep in beer, the women part is more of a pipe dream. Anyway, everyone's favorite internet PR guy announced some new nerfs...err...<a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum2/HTML/001258.html">policies going into effect on the official EQ Boards</a>.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Hello all, <br><br>We're quite pleased with the way the boards are working out so far, and hope that they will continue in this fashion. That said, there are a couple other issues that we need to address in order to facilitate the board's continued usefulness: <br><br>Nerf Requests: We're going to begin closing requests to nerf others classes. It becomes a fairly common occurance when it's apparent that we aren't going to upgrade another class. Nerf requests are very inflamatory and are a breeding ground for all-out flame wars. As we don't want to have to liberally ban people if it can be handled via other means, closing the threads is probably the best action we could take. <br><br>Dead issues: We'll also begin closing threads, explicitly or implicitly addressed to us, that we consider dead issues, issues that we've addressed already and consider 'locked down'. You all can feel free to continue discussing the issue amongst yourselves, but if it's a 'Verant please read!' thread, and we consider the issue closed, we'll close the thread as well. We're going to do this in hopes of making room for new threads on other subjects that just can't seem to draw much interest on their first go-around. Rather than have a dozen threads pop up asking us to continue explaining the issue, this might be the best course of action. <br><br>In addition, I'm going to create a 'dead issue' section of the FAQ for these things as they continue to come up. We realize that not everyone can read everything on the boards every day, so we should have the data available someplace. <br><br>-Gordon</font><br><br>What kind of A-hole requests that someone elses class be nerfed? I know my Ranger isn't the most powerful of the classes, and judging by a lot of posts it may be the weakest, but I don't want Necros nerfed to compensate for my shortcomings.<br><br>Dead issues = anything that Verant doesn't want to comment on. That's about all I will say on that one.<br><br>So Verant continues to nerf everything in site. They must be stopped at all costs! I swear I expect to wake up tomorrow and see this posted somewhere "PC's deemed too powerful will be nerfed. If you computer is above a PIII 600 with 128MB/ram (otherwise known as 'powerful enough to actually enjoy Kunark') it will be replaced with a P200 with 32MB or ram. We found that players with fast computers have an unfair advantage over other players. Likewise, if you have a cable modem or above our technicians will be over to remove it and install a 28.8k modem. Fast internet connections are found to be an unfair advantage for some players."<br><br>All this as the earth floats around in space. It's crazy.</p>
<a name="newsitem965401947,47740,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">A Top List that doesn't suck</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, August 4, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">From one list to another, today just keeps getting better. This list is actually cool though. One of my favorite current sites is <a href="http://x-entertainment.com"><b>X-Entertaiment</b></a>(not to be confused with the sort of X entertainment you get at the local adult film theater. Not that I have ever been to one. Or at least been to one often. Well, I don't frequent them. Ok, I am writing this from one right now! You satisfied?).<br><br>Anyway, X-Entertainment has the <a href="http://www.x-entertainment.com/messages/334.html"><b>Top 12 Star Wars figures</b></a> ever! This kind of list is so me. When I was a kid I spent many of days playing with my Star Wars collection. I had more Star Wars stuff then I knew what to do with. I once suckered my friend into giving me all his Star Wars stuff, which also included the much coveted Millenium Falcon, for a couple of slot car tracks. What a sucker!<br><br>One of the darkest days in the history of my life is when my dad, god bless his soul, gave my entire toy collection to the neighbors kid because they were poor and couldn't afford to buy him stuff. I was devastated. Not only my Star Wars stuff, but my entire Transformers and He-Man collection too! Not that I was playing with them much at the time, I was like 16, but those are the things you kind of want to keep forever. Ah well, hopefully that brat that ended up with my X-Wing fighter (with battle damage) appreciated the stuff. <br><br>Now my entire toy collection consists of the items that are sitting on my work desk. A Darth Maul figure, a mini-Millenium Falcon and Charmander of Pokemon fame. Don't ask.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000008.html"><b>The first person to e-mail me and say this has nothing to do with Everquest gets thumped in the head.</B></a> </p>
