<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">What to do?</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, August 3, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Recently I was approached with an offer to move EQ Rants. Someone wants to host my site and actually pay me to be on their servers. The money isn't too great, it is actually not even really good, but it is actually not the main focus here. <br><br>The main thing is that they will cross promote the site on some of their other sites. I don't want to get caught up in the "how many hits did I get today" thing, but the fact is that anyone who runs a website wants people to read their stuff. EQ Rants started off as me joking around and grew, just a little bit, bigger then that. I think it would be fun to have quite a few more people reading the site. Not that you regulars aren't enough or anything. But I am certain that Kithias would like more people reading Eversticks, and so would I.<br><br>I would also have the opportunity to host other sites right here at EQ Rants, which would lead to more content. And in my opinion more content is a good thing. Let's face facts, web pages with no content are rather boring.<br><br>Of course this would come with a price, I would have to slap a couple of add banners on the site. I hate to think of being a sellout, but sometimes you have to hop at an opportunity.<br><br>The reason I am posting this is because I want your opinions. You are the reason that EQ Rants has had any level of success. I guess I had maybe a little to do with it, but if you guys didn't read my stuff then I would just have a site of me talking to myself. Let me know what you think, either via <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.com"><b>e-mail</B></a> or by this convenient <a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000006.html"><b>Ranting Board link</b></a>.</p>
