<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Patch Rant</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, August 2, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Yesterday Verant patched, which means today you get a patch rant. This patch is extremely boring which is going to make this patch rant really hard to write. Just like I do with the rest of this site, I am completely writing off the top of my head here. If this totally sucks I apologize.<br><br>Not really.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Greetings everyone!  <br><br>Today's patch contains some changes that we are sure everyone will enjoy:<br><br>- Canned emotes (e.g. /point) now work on NPCs.  In addition, the range for canned emotes has been increased.</font><br><br>- Great, I can sit there and emote at a computer character that doesn't respond nor care about me in the least bit. I can picture the hours of fun laughing at NPC's.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- /who all 'guildname' should now work for players who have /roleplay turned on.<br>- Preferences for the mouselook will be saved in your options file.  Those who turn mouselook off each time when starting EQ will only have to do it once more.</font><br><br>- Any chance of the same thing ever happening for run?<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The 'Chat Filter' tab in 'Options' now has an option to filter messages caused by damage shields hitting others.<br><br>*Fast Drop*<br><br>Our most exciting change today is an option that allows players to avoid accidentally dropping items on the ground.  The new client allows players to set 'Item Dropping' preferences on the 'General' options tab.  The three options that can be set are:<br><br>- FAST DROP: Items are dropped without confirmation.<br>- CONFIRM: A confirmation box will be displayed whenever you try to drop an item.<br>- NEVER: You are not allowed to drop items on the ground.  <br><br>Alternatively, you can also set these options using the /fastdrop command.  The arguments are:<br><br>- ON: Same as option 'Fast Drop' on the General Tab.<br>- OFF: Same as option 'Confirm' on the General Tab.<br>- NEVER: Same as above.<br><br>Please note that whatever your setting, coin will always be dropped without confirmation.  Additionally, the FastDrop option only applies to items being dropped upon the ground.  Handing items to NPCs will still work regardless of your FastDrop setting.<br><br>It is highly recommended that you use option 'CONFIRM', as GMs will not reimburse any items that are accidentally dropped.</font><br><br>Thus totally making the player accountable for Verant bugs. If you accidentally drop something to the ground and it vanishes due to a bug, it is your own fault. Remember all that stuff a while ago about Verant taking the players word and replacing items and then looking into teh situation. Well that lasted all of a day I think. On the very same day Gordon said there was a misunderstanding and the policy was changed. Now they add this. On top of that they try to mask it as being an "Exciting new feature". An exciting new feature is mana and heal potions at NPC vendors. This is garbage.<br><br>Ok, I know a lot of people actually might like this change. Especially bards who must frequently switch items in and out of their hands. Just a big part of me things Verant did this to save them from having to replace items, and not to make things easier on the players.<br><br>Yes, I am a cynical bastard.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">- The EverQuest Team</font> <br><br>- The EQ Rants Team<br><br></p>
