<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Official Boards...they are changing</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, August 1, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I really hate when <a href="http://lumthemad.net"><b>Lum</b></a> beats me to this stuff. It's not as though I don't already have a "Lum ripoff" complex as it is. But hey, Lum and I are great pals so he won't mind. Actually we aren't great pals, but he doesn't mind me and I don't mind him. Am I still talking?<br><br>Anyway, I was going to post this yesterday, but I was too worn out from apartment shopping. Yes, walking into an apartment to decide if I want to live there or not wears me out. But that is, again, besides the point. <br><br>Any bets on when I will actually get to the point?<br><br>Ok, we'll start the point here.<br><br>I know we have a strict "Don't quote Abashi" all the time rule, but I'll break that for this kind of stuff. This comes straight from the official message boards (no links, too lazy).<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Hello everyone,<br><br>We are pleased to announce that tomorrow we will be implementing some major changes here on the boards. While everyone will remain able to read all of the forums, they will be restricted so that only active EverQuest account holders will have the right to post. It's important that we mention that though we respect the opinion of those who no longer play EverQuest, these forums are provided as a service for active customers. The change will allow us to service existing subscribers to a greater extent.<br><br>At the same time that these changes are made, we will begin strict moderation of the boards. The flames and personal attacks that are now so common on these boards will no longer be allowed to continue. As posters will have to log in with their active EverQuest account info, we will have all the tools necessary to track down and take action upon posters who choose to engage in some of the less-than-courteous banter that takes place here. We will also be posting a FAQ that not only explains the new rules that will be observed and enforced on the boards, but also goes into verbose explanation of some of the issues that come up here quite regularly (e.g. melee binding, experience requirements, etc.) <br><br>As a symbol of our renewed committment to return the boards to a standard of acceptability, we will be completely wiping the boards at the time of the change. <br><br>Below is a subset of the FAQ that will be made available tomorrow regarding the new rules on the board:<br><br>---snip---<br>General Rules for EverQuest Forums<br><br>As the Official EverQuest Forums are part of The Station, posting to these forums is bound by The Station's Terms of Service that can be found in their entirety at <a href="http://www.station.sony.com/services/tos.jhtml.">http://www.station.sony.com/services/tos.jhtml.</a> In addition to these terms of service, we have a few supplemental rules that apply to the EverQuest Forums.<br><br>In general, you may post any material, written in a courteous and mature manner, providing that it is on-topic for the forum to which you are posting. This includes material that disagrees with the way that we, the developers, operate the game. We will not interfere with the communication of thoughts and ideas as long as the presentation is appropriate for all those capable of reading the forum.<br><br>You may not, however, post any material that:<br><br>· Attacks or insults others on the board. Feel free to debate the idea, but do not turn your disagreement into an attack upon the poster.<br>· Engages in name-calling, harassment, or threats. See above.<br>· Contains obscenity, vulgarity, or profanity. Though we do have a filter in place to catch the unintentional obscenity from time to time, this is not a license to abuse it.<br>· Disparages any religion, race, nation, gender, or sexual orientation. <br>· Is considered inappropriate for children 13 or over as governed by general standards of decency in the United States.<br>· Infringes on anyone's privacy rights.<br><br>Furthermore, you may not:<br><br>· Make multiple posts on the same subject for the purpose of getting attention paid to your issue.<br>· Post off-topic comments in threads for the purpose of drawing attention to another thread on a different subject.<br>· Monopolize the front page of any forum by "bumping" threads of the same or similar content to the front. We may intervene by closing threads any time that this occurs.<br>· Use the official forums as a staging-ground for creating general unrest within the game (e.g. Sit-ins).<br>· Use the official forums as a place to advertise the sale of EverQuest characters or items in exchange for real-world money.<br>· Advertise web-sites with content that violates these rules, the EverQuest EULA, or the Station Terms of Service.<br>· Advertise products or websites that are not related to EverQuest or other Verant/Sony Online Entertainment products.<br><br>Actions Taken For Violation<br><br>Action that we might take in regards to a post in violation of these rules on the Official EverQuest Forums will vary depending upon the transgression. It could include any number of the following:<br><br>· Editing of the post.<br>· Deletion of the post/thread.<br>· Closing of the thread.<br>· Suspension (results in user being unable to play EverQuest for the duration of the suspension).<br>· Banishment (results in the user's station account being canceled. User will no longer be able to access EverQuest, or any Official EverQuest Forum).<br>· Legal Action (i.e. Contacting law enforcement personnel in regard to a threat.)<br><br>People who violate the rules of the boards may or may not receive any warning before any action is taken. In the event that a warning is given, the warning will be recorded upon the game account and may result in further action should the player show a pattern of engaging in prohibited conduct. Philosophically and administratively, there is no difference between conduct in game, and conduct in the Official EverQuest Forums.<br>---snip---<br><br>As a note, we will begin strictly enforcing these rules as soon as the changes are made. We would like to ask for everyone's cooperation in following and enforcing these rules at that time.<br><br>Thank you,<br><br>Gordon Wrinn</font> <br><br>In case you don't frequent the <a href="http://http://boards.station.sony.com/ubb/everquest/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro"><b>official boards</b></a>(now you get a link) let me fill you in on what goes on there. Basically everyone bitches and complains that 'X class is overpowered while Z class is underpowered'. While this goes on valid complaints and problems tend to get ignored. <br><br>Verant taking an active step in cleaning up the boards is a good thing, in my opinion. I don't agree with all of their means of achieving this, but with Verant you have to take the good with the bad. I think it is on page 57 of 'The Vision' (coming soon to paperback!). <br><br>I really don't agree with them having the ability to ban our account if they don't like what you post on the board. I think I will stop posting there immediately. I also don't like how they will moderate the boards by deleting/editing threads and posts that they think are in violation of their rules. To me it seems like a way for them to avoid answering anything that they don't want to answer. Well, currently they achieve that by just ignoring the thread anyway...so what the hell is the difference right?<br><br>Anyway, I have rambled on about this long enough. Verant is nerfing the boards now, next they will attempt to nerf your keyboard. <br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum7/HTML/000005.html"><b>Feel free to comment, I haven't left one of these links up in a while.</b></a> (it's all because of that Lum ripoff complex dammit)</p>
