<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Milo Says</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, July 31, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I saw that Everlore (no link as I refuse to link to them twice in one day) had another one of the popular Ask Milo updates today. I personally don't think much of Milo. He is condescending and sometimes just rude. Today in his update we got this gem.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">It takes so long for the techies at Verant to fix bugs such as the one that is currently plauging many of us the one that kicks us off Eq back to the server select screen every 10 minutes. Are they really trying or they just taking a vacation with the 2.5 million they recieve every month?<br><br>Deek <br><br>Milo Says: <br>We game makers leave bugs in our software so the whiny dork sites have something to talk about.</font> <br><br>As usual he blows off anyone that wants to bring up a valid complaint with the game, much like what happens on the official EQ messageboards. The author of the letter could have left out the vacation part and just asked why things take so long to get fixed, but I understand where he is coming from. Bugs do take a long time to get fixed, way too long in some cases. But like Milo said, if they fixed it correctly whiny <a href="http://eqrants.net"><b>dork</b></a> <a href="http://lumthemad.net"><b>sites</b></a> wouldn't have anything to talk about. Much like if Abashi never posted on the messageboards, none of the news sites would have anything to talk about. At least our sites can always talk about the piss-poor customer support and the assinine idea of 'The Vision'.<br><br>But what do I know, I am just a whiny <a href="http://eqrants.net/now.jpg"><b>dork</b></a>.</p>
