<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Diablo II Stuff</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, July 18, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Yesterday I decided to try playing Diablo II on Battle.net. I played through the game in single player mode originally because I had read the horror stories about battle.net. Let me tell you, they are all true.<br><br>I started off by making a new character, an amazon. I don't know why an amazon, just seemed like a good idea at the time. I tried to name my amazon. After the first 20 names I tried were 'Rejected by the Server'. I finally gave up and decided to type in the most ridiculous name I could think of, hence HoeTrain was born. Yes, the game rejected a ton of 'Roleplaying' type names that I threw at it, but accepted HoeTrain with loving arms.<br><br>I logged HoeTrain onto the USEast server and tried to create my own game. Bad move. I was given a message that this wasn't going to be possible and that I should join someone else's game instead. Alright, will do. I found a server that had some low level characters on it and proceeded to find some stuff to kill. Instead what I found was lag, a whole lot of it. I haven't seen lag that bad since the early days of Ultima Online. For those of you who weren't around during the early days of Ultima Online, let me tell you...it was pretty bad. I trudged forth anyway, determined to play. I found some other players and we started a little group. Apart from the lag that would send me back and forth like some sort of involuntary teleport spell, things seemed ok. The group met up for a big run at a boss monster. <br><br>I was then kicked off of the server.<br><br>I turned off Diablo II and proceeded to smash my fingers with a mallet. It was actually less painful then trying to play on battle.net.<br><br>Those of you who think Diablo II is an Everquest killer are sadly mistaken.</p>
<a name="newsitem963835195,87114,"></a>
<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Odds and ends</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, July 17, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I beat Diablo II over the weekend. Now I can get back to my mission of getting my ranger to level 20 on EQ. Diablo II was/is a fun game, as soon as Worthless manages to finish it hopefully we can get a full review up for it. Reviewing games isn't really our thing, but what the hell, for our readers we'll give it a whirl regardless.<br>---<br><br>Over the weekend I went to a bachelor party for one of my lifelong best friends. A big group of my friends, who hadn't really been together in years, got together and went out to celebrate my friends final days of bachelorhood. We, of course, hit nekkid bars. I mean, where else do you go for a bachelor party? <br><br>After hitting a nice little nekkid club here in the States, we headed to Canada. You see, in Canada the girls get completely nude. Here in Michigan they don't. Well the club in Canada kinda sucked. We all agreed on that. We were going to go somewhere else but we had to wait for the bachelor to get some shower dance with some of the strippers. <br><br>Three of my friends apparently weren't having a good time. Instead of trying to make the best of it, they just left. They had no car, they were just going to find a way home. They didn't tell the bachelor anything about it. They just disappeared without a trace. Oh, and on their way out they assigned me with the task of breaking the news to the bachelor that they were leaving. Here is what they told me to say "Don't tell him that we are going back to Michigan, just say that you don't know where we went but you know that we will find our own way home and not to worry about us." Worry about you? How about fuck you!<br><br>Instead of just dealing with one bad club, they up and left.  Totally bailing on the bachelor and his night out to be with 'The Guys', his best friends from high school. Oh, one of the guys is actually standing up in the wedding next week. I couldn't imagine having to look at him and try to explain why I bailed on the bachelor party. It's all pretty sad.<br><br>I guess the worst part about this is the realization that three of my supposed best friends are completely selfish bastards. Maybe that is what happens when you get older. You're friends stop giving a shit about anyone else and only worry about serving themselves. I would love to take on that philosophy, but I just can't do it. I am not that big of an asshole. Although some people at Verant may disagree.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum2/HTML/000017.html"><b>Yes, that was completely off topic but I had to vent.</b></a> </p>
