<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Taking it too far</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, July 11, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I know there is a lot of hatred for Abashi, and for the EQ team in general. I know that most everyone thinks that Verant, as a company, is incompetent and not worth the CD's that they put their games on. I run a website based on those things alone. I feel we have every right to speak our mind about a game that we continually pay to beta test. We should have free reign to state our opinion, be it good or bad, at any time. No holds barred style. As long as we keep it about the game.<br><br>Unfortunately people can't stop there. There are now pictures of Abashi, from the EQ gathering in Vegas, floating around the web. Not to be mean about it, but Abashi is obviously a big guy. Hey, I know lot's of big guys, big deal. We aren't all the same. Well some of the people on the <a href="http://boards-cgi.station.sony.com/everquest/cgi-bin/forumdisplay.cgi?action=topics&forum=Gameplay&number=4&DaysPrune=10&LastLogin="><b>EQ Bitchfest</b></a> have taken the opportunity to run down Abashi and make personal attacks on him based on his weight. This has nothing to do with Everquest, it is just being mean. I like to poke fun and generally say not nice things about the guys at Verant. The difference is I never make personal attacks on them. You have to know where the line is. It is just a game remember. The people that would make fun of him for his appearance take the game way too seriously. <br><br>I noticed some people thought over what they said and apologized for it. I guess that is at least the right thing to do, but it shouldn't have come to that in the first place. The guy goes to Vegas to meet with the players, knowing full well that a lot of them despise him. He gets to come back and read a message board with posts ridiculing him for things not game related.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum2/HTML/000015.html"><b>Some of you people are just plain sad.</b></a> </p>
