<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">EQ Stratics wants your help</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, July 11, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I noticed that <a href="http://eq.stratics.com"><b>EQ Stratics</b></a> is advertising some positions for their little site. Of course they have a few requirements such as:<br><br>- You must be 18 years of age or older<br><br>- Have good language skills<br><br>- Can commit to at least 5 hours a week<br><br>- Are constantly searching for new news about EverQuest OR<br><br>- Are kept "in the know" on your server about upcoming events<br><br>Now, I figure this job should be easy for about 95% of the people out there. If you get rid of all the BS requirements, it pretty much comes down to this.<br><br>- You must post news that other sites have already reported.<br><br>- You must be willing to post every word that Gordon says on any messageboard.<br><br>Now I know I am rather hard on some of these "news sites". Maybe I am a bit bitter because many of them have completely blown me off in the past. Maybe they don't want to ruin their relationships with Verant by posting a link to a site that's primary goal is to point out every flaw in their game.<br><br>Or maybe I am just an asshole.</p>
