<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">*a expansion pack hits you for $30 worth of damage.* </font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, July 10, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">In an effort to draw attention away from the current game bugs and various other problems, Brad McQuaid has announced a new expansion for EQ. The expansion will take place on the continent of Velious, which is an ice land. It will be full of your basic ice creatures I suppose, ice dragons, ice giants, snow bunnies, ice cream trucks. You know, typical stuff that would normally be found in Antarctica. <br><br>The expansion will also feature new player models, but apparently no new playable classes or races. It also appears it won't add any additional levels. Everyone will still be stuck at 60. Bummer. It apparently will feature a new city for Barbarians. The expansion should be ready by December. Which means we will most likely see it in March.<br><br>I certainly hope this means that they plan on fixing the bugs that currently exist. You know that the expansion will introduce a whole new slew of bugs (and not the mosquito type that exist in Daikatana).<br><br>Unfortunately the EQ Online Store probably won't be available again until next April. Hopefully by that time everyone who ordered Kunark will have received it.<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum2/HTML/000014.html"><b>Comment on this, if you feel like it.</b></a> </p>
