<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Diablo II/Everquest</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, July 7, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">So far so good, I am actually enjoying Diablo II. Sometimes non-stop action is actually a good thing. Not having to stop to stare at a spell book every few minutes is a good thing. Not camping for an item is a good thing. Being able to fight 10 monsters at once and not dying is a good thing. <br><br>I know that comparing Diablo II and Everquest is like comparing apples and beef, they aren't even in the same group, but Diablo II does have some thing that EQ should have. Mana potions? Healing potions? Would these things really be that hard to include in EQ? Have a little vendor in every city that sells potions. You don't even have to make them cheap, just make them available. Would it be a bad thing if players didn't have to spend so much time staring at a spellbook or sitting and healing for 5+ minutes. I personally don't think so. I think it would make the game a ton more fun for casual gamers like myself. And I am quite certain the power gamers would enjoy it to. Half of the time I play EQ I just get discouraged because it is extremely tedious.<br><br>I actually meant to spend more time talking about Diablo II in this post. I just got off track and remembered how annoying EQ can be.<br><br></p>
