<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">We now return you to your regularly scheduled idiocy</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, July 6, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I know, I said I was back two days ago. Well yesterday I decided to keep myself busy by doing absolutely nothing productive. I figured that after 4 days in the woods surrounded by bugs, raccoons and morons, it was the least I deserved. So I spent my day actually playing EQ. I figure it is sort of, you know, a prerequisite to running an EQ website. No major gripes with EQ right now. I did run into a nasty little bug though. I was trading items with a friend and in the middle of the trade of we both got kicked right back to the desktop. What was real fun is that we were standing in the middle of Unrest at the time. No deaths or anything resulted, I'll just chalk it up to another Verant programming error. Sometimes I wonder if this game hasn't been coded with an <a href="http://www.etch-a-sketch.com/"><b>Etch-A-Sketch</b></a>.<br><br>I am extremely out of the news loop as of right now. I will do my normal scannings of sites in a bit and post anything that I feel is rantworthy. I am going to go out on a limb and say that most of the other sites covered the latest thing that Abashi had for breakfast while I was gone. <br><br>A quick thanks to <a href="mailto:worthles@eqrants.net"><b>worthless</b></a> for taking care of the site while I was gone. He doesn't post as often as I do, but he also doesn't whine, bitch and complain as much as me either. Actually very few people do.... <br></p>
