<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">*a raving buur slashes at you for 52 points of damage.*</font> </strong><small>Posted Saturday, July 1, 2000 by <a href="mailto:worthles@eqrants.net">worthless</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">Well, it's saturday, that means Buur has been away from the computer for 2 days now. Anyone care to wager how many more days he will last? I'm give him till noon tomorrow, then he will either;<br><br>     A) Go insane, killing everything in site... or<br>     B) Escape the woods and run to the nearest best buy.<br><br>Camping ugh... I dunno, I guess I've never found sitting around in the woods, swatting mosquitoes, and eating trail mix very fun. I don't care what anyone says, it is not a real vacation unless there is a TV and a lot of cold beer handy ;)<br><br>On the EQ news front... I'm sure most of you heard, or read, or were affected by the test server wipe(myself included in this last group, having lost a character I was quite fond of)... This whole issue has just gotten out of hand. First they deleted all the characters on test, then they bring the characters back and delete the items, then they allow the characters to move, without items, to another server, now they are taking the moved characters back to Test server. Read all about it <b><a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum4/HTML/058382.html">here</a></b>. For those of you whose primary characters were on the test server, you have my sympathy. I totally agree with Verant that the test server needed to be cleaned up a bit, BUT the way this was handled should NEVER have happened. These players have put just as much time in to their characters as anyone else, and if nothing else they at least deserved a planned out procedure, rather than this random bullshit that has happened.</p>
