<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Imagine</font> </strong><small>Posted Wednesday, June 28, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I just read this at <a href="http://eqanswers.com">EQ Answers</a>. Apparently yesterday Verant did a little test on the aptly named Test Center. What they tested was a dungeon that actually had, hold on to your seats, random spawns!<br><br>The players were told to go to the Arena and upon entering they were confronted with animals all over. After they were done killing them all they got a message saying <font color="#FFFF00">"Congratulations on the first ever test of a Dynamic Dungeon in Everquest"</font>.<br><br>My god, can it possibly be true that someone over at Verant finally realized that camping is an issue? I know the farmers and campers would cry their eyes out but this would be great for the casual gamer, such as myself. If they could apply something like this to the whole world it would be a complete breakthrough. If they could get rid of zone lines it would be a perfect game for me. Well, that and if they stopped nerfing stuff. This reminds me of a song I once heard.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">Image there's no camping, it's easy if you try. No waiting for spawns, just be careful, don't die. Imagine all the players, wandering happily.<br><br>Imagine there are no zone lines, it isn't hard to do. No need to wait for loading times, and no lock-ups too. Imagine all the people, not reading Loading...Please Wait.<br><br>Imagine no nerfing, I wonder if you can. No need to bitch or complain, we would all love Verant. Imagine all the people, being content with EQ. <br><br>You may say I'm a dreamer, but I'm not the only one. I hope some day you'll join us. And the world will be as one.</font> <br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum2/HTML/000012.html"><b>Those may not be the lyrics to the song I am thinking of, but close enough</b></a> </p>
