<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">EQG3</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, June 20, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">In our continuing effort to out-scoop all the major, Verant friendly, news sites, we, once again, broke out the old time machine.<br><br>This time worthless and myself traveled to <b><a href="http://www.solosnet.com/tourney/refs.cfm?site=61" target="_blank">Sin</a></b> City to see how <a href="http://eqgathering.bizland.com/"><b>EQG3</b></a> went. Much to our dismay, it wasn't pretty.<br><br><center><img src="http://eqrants.net/riots.jpg"></center><br><br>Apparently things got violent after Verant officials continued to insist that "The game is fine" and that "Rangers are viable after level 50".<br><br>One distraught player had this to say, "Do they take us for fools?! The game has problems, can't they just fix it?! And on top of that, they ran out of beer."<br><br>One man, who identified himself only as <a href="http://www.worthless.net/alabamaman2.jpg"><b>Alabama Man</b></a>, said this, "I aint got much schoolin, but momma always said when you see a bug you should squash it. Didn't thems momma's ever teachem anything?"<br><br>Eventually things calmed down. There were 13 arrests and no major injuries. Afterwards Gordon Wrynn released the following statement, "All things considered, we feel the event was a success. We were able to meet many of our players face to face and get a general feeling for our player base. We have determined that they are all wackos and this will be the last player gathering that myself, or anyone else from Verant, ever attends. You people are sick!!! I thought psychos only played Ultima Online!!! Oh, and don't forget to check out our new expansion, the Ruins of Kunark! Complete with new lands and a new playable race! You can order it from our online store!"<br><br><a href="http://www.eqrants.net/ubb/Forum2/HTML/000007.html"><b>I feel another riot coming on...</b></a> </p>
