<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Letter to Lucas Arts</font> </strong><small>Posted Monday, June 19, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">As many of you should know, Verant is going to do Star Wars Online for Lucas Arts. This has many Star Wars Geeks (no offense, I am one myself) and curent EQ players worried. They have images of falling through Tatooine or having to take a half hour ride from one planet to the next on the broken transport shuttle. One player decided to address his concerns directly to Lucas Arts. You can read that letter <a href="http://boards.station.sony.com/everquest/Forum4/HTML/053362.html"><b>here</b></a> (I would post it here but it is way to frickin' long).<br><br>He posts some pretty valid points regarding EQ. Although there is nothing really new that we haven't said before. Yes, EQ is buggy. Yes, EQ has questionable customer support. Yes, Verant's  employees are spawns from hell. Err...wait, Abashi said they weren't and he has no reason to lie to me.<br><br>Anyway, the problem is that this one letter will make no difference. It would take 1000's and 1000's of letters just like that one (from different people mind you) to put a worry in Lucas Arts mind. For as much as I, and many, many others, like to bitch about EQ, the general public loves it. The people that bitch and complain are not the EQ common public. All of us on newsgroups and <a href="http://www.eqrants.net/cgi-bin/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro">message boards</a> are way in the minority. Not only will Lucas Arts see that, but Verant knows it. Their bread and butter is in the customers who don't complain and don't bitch. You know, the ones that just play the game to have a good time (amazingly enough, these people exist. I even know some of them). Verant doesn't have to cater to the whiners when the general public is content with the game. <br><br>In the end, unfortunately, that well written letter will accomplish nothing. It is truly a valiant effort on the authors part, but Lucas Arts isn't going to care. And we already know that Verant doesn't care, right?</p>
