<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">Me first, me first!!!!</font> </strong><small>Posted Friday, June 16, 2000 by <a href="mailto:worthles@eqrants.net">worthless</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">We here at EQRants are dedicated to being the first to bring you Abashi posts straight from the EQ message board. In our effort to remain ahead of the pack, we kidnapped world renowned "mad scientist" Doc Brown, locked him in our basement, and performed chinese water torture until he gave us the secret of the flux capacitor. Using this incredible new technology we traveled many years into the future, what we found both shocked and amazed us... Jaded with the EQ lifestyle, Abashi left Verant and took employment with a national newspaper. Without further ado, we present to you... direct from the San Diego Enquirer, "Dear Abashi!"<br><br>Dear Abashi:<br><br>My wife and I have been online married for 3 years now. We have lost the spark in our cyber romance. What can we do to regain the spirit and energy of our youth?<br><br>Sincerely,<br>Depressed in Yahoo Chat<br><br><font color="yellow">Dear Depressed in Yahoo! Chat:<br><br>As married life sets in it is easy to get set in your routines, and to in turn get stuck in a romantic rut. Sometimes the best way to rekindle a dwindling relationship is a change of scenery. Here's what you do... email your wife a mysterious URL and tell her to meet there at exactly 8pm... and no peeking! When 8pm rolls around she will load up the URL and find a beautiful pink chat room, complete with romantic midi music and possibly a flickering candle java applet. If you follow these steps accordingly, I guarantee you will reawaken the passion in your online experience.<br><br>~Abashi</font><br><br>-------------<br><br>Dear Abashi:<br><br>I cannot stay on top of the cyber lingo! I sit around in chat and have no idea what anyone is saying! ROFL, LMAO, BRB? What does it all mean? Is it short hand? French? Binary? How can I be as cool as my AOL friends?<br><br>Sincerely,<br>confused in private room: ereet<br><br><font color="yellow">Dear Confused:<br><br>Proper use of slang is essential to cybercoolness. Until you are down with the lingo of the net you will be the object of anger and ridicule from your AOL compatriots. I suggest you read the best selling classic "I kiss you: sexy turkish man's guide to the internet" By Majir.<br><br>~Abashi</font><br><br>-------------<br><br>Dear Abashi:<br><br>Being an elite hax0r is a full time job. I barely have time to check my email, let alone mow the lawn or feed the cat. It has been years since I have seen the sun, my hair is greasy, my skin is pail and worst of all I have begun to develop a rash from sitting in this sweaty chair all day. What do I do?<br><br>Sincerely,<br>Dennis<br><br><font color="yellow">Dear Dennis:<br><br>Two words... Topical Cream<br><br>~Abashi</font><br><br>-------------<br><br>Dear Abashi:<br><br>Several years ago when I first discovered the net I could surf for pron all day and not be phased. In recent years my pron habit has developed into an obsession. I am afraid that I am harming my family, and I am afraid that I am harming myself. Please help!<br><br>Sincerely,<br>Rigid in Detroit<br><br><font color="yellow">Dear Buur:<br><br>Two words... Topical Cream<br><br>~Abashi</font><br><br>-------------<br><br>This concludes our peek into the future. Check back soon for another riveting installment.</p>
