<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">My evening in Everquest</font> </strong><small>Posted Thursday, June 15, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">I haven't done one of these in a while, so I thought it might be time for another addition of:<br><br><b>Buur's EQ Life</B> (never mind that I have never done this before, just play along)<br><br>The evening started off pretty typical. I logged in with my Iskar Shaman and was off to kick some ass. I am quite possibly the most unreliable group member in history, so I was soloing as usual. I headed toward the Field of Bone, where most everyone else on the server seems to be on most nights. Almost immediately I was attacked by a bandit. Excellent, it conned blue, shouldn't be a problem at all. After giving the bandit the beat down of his life (which, considering the fact that they don't tend to live too long after spawning, was the only beat down of his life) he turned tail and started running. I chased after him with my trusty cracked staff (I have the suckiest weapons in the world) and was immediately attacked by another bandit and a scalebone skeleton. Well I had SoW on so I started running. SoW expired. I started running not as fast. As I got into the woods the framerate started crawling. Turns out EQ doesn't run so good with a V5, when you have 4x FSAA enabled and the clipping plane all the way up. I expired. Loading...Please Wait. Ran back to my body, got my stuff, /q.<br><br>I logged on with my main character on Xegony, aptly named Buur. Immediately I contacted one of my friends online. Turns out she was on the other side of the world (and yes, believe it or not, <a href="http://www.solosnet.com/tourney/refs.cfm?site=61"><b>she</b></a> is a real <a href="http://www.solosnet.com/tourney/refs.cfm?site=61"><b>she</b></a>). I started asking, very politely mind you, for a quick teleport to Karana. "Anyone going to Karana, I'll gladly pay for gas if I can hitch a ride". No response. I was in Greater Faydark mind you, no shortage of druids. I watched a few of them pull a wolf form right in front of me, as if to mock me. After some repeated, humorous, attempts to get a teleport I gave in to begging for one. Still no go. People on Xegony, you suck!! <br><br>After two hours of futility, I finally gave up. Two hours of my life that I will never get back. Two hours of my life that I could have spent looking up porn or playing TFC. Ack.</p>
