<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">I have changed dammit!!!!</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, June 13, 2000 by <a href="mailto:buur@eqrants.net">Buur</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3">As if to totally reassure everyone that <a href="http://www.drtwsiter.com">The Dr. Twister Network</a> has changed, the good doctor posted this on his <a href="http://eq.drtwister.com">EQ site</a>.<br><br><font color="#FFFF00">As a reminder to everyone, we are beginning to assist in the tracking of bugs in order to help relieve some of the work from the EQ team. If you have information, please feel free to share it with us. We will make sure we get it into the appropriate hands in order for it to be fixed, and in return, should have a status on when we should expect the bug to be fixed. WE WILL NOT POST THE STEPS IN WHICH TO DUPLICATE THE BUG.</font> <br><br>That is quite different then his former policy. It mainly consisted of putting every known bug out there, in detail,  for everyone to try. The effect would be to totally mess up the game and make the companies in charge (Verant, Origin) fix them. The side effect was that said companies got a bit upset with him (see Origin, Lawsuit).<br><br>Doc Twisty has gone all legit on us. Is this a sign of the apocalypse. Nah, nothing that extreme. He just possibly saw the errors of his ways and now realizes there is a better way to go about thing then to piss a bunch of people off.</p>
