<p><font face="Arial" size="4" color="#4E657C">EQ for the P2?</font> </strong><small>Posted Sunday, June 11, 2000 by <a href="mailto:holychit@hotmail.com">worthless</a></small><br><font face="Arial" size="3"><font color="yellow">Disclaimer: It is now 6am and I have yet to sleep... Please excuse any errors in spelling/structure/logic.</font><br><br>I read the other day that Verant is looking for people to help develop a "next generation console" based game. Now, Verant is strictly a massively multiplayer game company, and the PS2 has broadband and modem support... remember about a year ago when the Playstation 2 was first anounced? There was talk of a possible Everquest port for the PS2, I wonder if that is the "next gen console" game they are developing. Unless you have been living under a rock you know that the PS2 has amazing graphics, imagine EQ in full anti-aliased glory... this could be very cool... NO MORE JAGGED LINES! No more cardboard cutout trees!<br><br>I wonder if the EQ port will be compatible with the current EQ servers... this could be both good and bad. <a href="http://www.solosnet.com/tourney/refs.cfm?site=61" target="_blank">Good</a>, because you could buy the PS2 version of EQ and have your account and characters already there waiting for you... but, it could be REALLY <a href="http://www.purenrg.com/photo/pics/beth99/be0606_nikki_bill_amy_bed.jpg" target="_blank">BAD</a> for the overcrowding situation. Also, consoles attract a completely different type of gamer, the game might be very different with a large number of console only players subscribing. Not only do console only gamers have a different attitude towards gaming, but they also may have different interests. Verant will have to take the console gamer's interests into consideration with every change they make. If the console gamer's subscription base is larger than the comp based gamer's subscription rate, these decisions may not be in our favor.<br><br>Then again, the PS2 EQ may have a totally different network... this could be very good for the overcrowding issue... especially if they offer a one time only character transfer to the new PS2 servers. This may not be possible though if the new code is incompatible with the old. Also, I am not sure of the data saving capabilities of the PS2, I don't know how patches and the like would be handled. If patches are gonna be stored on the memory cards, well, that really limits the size available for patches, and would most likely mean the game would not expand, new items would not be introduced etc...<br><br>Maybe I'll stick with the comp based version...</p>
